अगस्त्यः|अगस्त्य
अगस्त्यः
1 = अगस्ति See above.
--2 N.
of Śiva.
--Comp.
--उदयः {1} the rise
of Canopus which takes place about
the end of Bhādra; with the rise
of this star the waters become
clear; cf. R. 4. 21 प्रससादोदयादंभः
कुंभयोनेर्महौजसः. {2} the 7th day of the
dark half of Bhādra.
--गीता [अगस्त्येन
गीता विद्याभेदः] N. of a sort of विद्या
mentioned in the Bhārata Śāntiparvan;
(pl.) Agastya's hymn.
--चारः [ष.
त.] the course of Canopus, the time
of its rise which ushers the Śarat
season and then every thing on
earth assumes a lovely appearance.
--तीर्थं N. of a celebrated Tīrtha
in the south.
--वटः N. of a holy
place on the Himālaya.
--संहिता
Agastya's collection of law.
