अतिवह्
अतिवह् {c1c} P. To carry over or
across. --Caus.
1 To spend, pass (as
time); किं वा मयापि न
दिनान्यतिवाहितानि Māl. 6. 13; अतिवाहयांबभूव त्रियामां
R. 9. 70; ऋतून् 19. 47.
--2 To let pass
over, get through successfully;
गुहाविसारीण्यतिवाहितानि मया
कथंचिद्घनगर्जितानि R. 13. 28 allowed to pass
over my head, endured; स
शापस्तेनातिवाहितः Ks. 33. 91.
--3 To rid
oneself of, elude, avoid;
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">Page0034-b+ 56</a>]
अस्मिंस्तमालविटपांधकारे प्रविश्य एनमतिवाहयावः
Ratn. 2 get out of his way, elude
his pursuit (and thus cheat him).
--4 To transplant, remove (to another
place), bring or carry over;
अलकामतिवाह्यैव वसतिं वसुसंपदां Ku. 6. 37.
--5 To follow, tread (as a path);
लोकातिवाहिते मार्गे Sarva.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाहः|अतिवाह
अतिवाहः [अतीत्य देहं अन्यदेहे वाहः प्रापणं
स. त.]
1 Passing or conveying of
the सूक्ष्मशरीर, the subtle principle of
life, to other bodies at the expiry of
good actions (अदृष्ट) contributing
to the enjoyment of worldly
pleasures.
--2 Carrying over.
