अद्वैत|अद्वैतः
अद्वैत a. [न. ब.]
1 Not dual; of one
or uniform nature, equable,
unchanging; ˚तं सुखदुःखयोः U. 1. 39.
--2
Matchless, peerless, sole, only, unique.
--तं
[न. त.]
1 Non-duality, identity;
especially that of Brahma with the
universe or with the soul, or of
soul and matter; See अद्वय also.
--2 The supreme or highest truth
or Brahma itself.
--3 N. of an
Upanishad; अद्वैतेन solely, without any
duplicity.
--Comp.
--आनंदः (अद्वय˚) {1}
the joy arising from a knowledge of
the identity of the universe and the
supreme spirit. {2} N. of an author
who, according to Colebrooke,
flourished at the close of the 15th century.
--वादिन् = अद्वयवादिन् q. v. above; a
Vedāntin.
