अधर्मः|अधर्म|अधर्म्म|अधर्म्मः
अधर्मः [न. त.]
1 Unrighteousness,
irreligion, impiousness, wickedness,
injustice; ˚दंडनं Ms. 8. 127 unjust
punishment; अधर्मेण unjustly, in an
improper way; यश्चाधर्मेण पृच्छति
Ms. 2. 111; an unjust act; a guilty or
wicked deed; sin; ˚चारिन् committing
unjust or unrighteous deeds; so
˚आत्मन् of an irreligious spirit; तदा
कथं ˚भीरुः Ś. 5; ˚मय full of
wickedness or sin; for definitions &c. of
धर्म and अधर्म See Tarka K. P. 19.
(धर्म and अधर्म are two of the 24
qualities mentioned in Nyāya,
and they pertain only to the soul.
They are the peculiar causes of
pleasure and pain respectively.
They are imperceptible, but inferred
from reasoning and from
transmigration.)
--2 N. of a Prajāpati or of an
attendant of the sun.
--र्मा
Unrighteousness personified.
--र्मं
Devoid of attributes, an epithet of
ब्रह्मन्.
--Comp.
--अस्तिकायः the
category of अधर्म, See अस्तिकाय.
