अध्वर्युः|अध्वर्यु|अध्वर्य्यु|अध्वर्य्युः
अध्वर्युः [अध्वरमधीते Nir.; अध्वर-क्यच्
--युच् ततोंऽत्याकारलोपः Tv.]
1 Any
officiating priest, technically
distinguished from होतृ, उद्गातृ and ब्रह्मन्. His
duty was “to measure the ground,
build the altar, prepare sacrificial
vessels, to fetch wood and water,
light the fire, bring the animal and
immolate it,” and while doing this
to repeat the Yajurveda; होता प्रथमं
शंसति तमध्वर्युः प्रोत्साहयति Sk. See अच्छावाक
also.
--2 The Yajurveda itself. --pl.
Adherents of that Veda.
--Comp.
--वेदः Yajurveda.
