<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग|अनुगः
अनुग a. [अनुगच्छतीति, गम्-ड] (In
comp.) Following, going after;
corresponding or tallying with,
adequate to; सदा पृष्ठानुगः पुरे Pt. 1. 59;
गीतानुगं वारि मृदंगवाद्यं R. 16. 64;
Me. 47; कामक्रोधवशानुगं Ms. 2. 214;
गोत्ररिक्थानुगः पिंडः 9. 142 governed or
regulated by; 8. 239.
--गः A
follower, (obedient) servant, companion;
तद्भूतनाथानुग R. 2. 58, 9. 82; बल˚
followed by an army, being the
head of an army.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगत|अनुगतः
अनुगत p. p.
1 (Used passively)
(a) Followed (lit. & fig.),
attended; अनुगतमलिवृंदैर्गंडभित्तीर्विहाय
R. 12. 102; M. 3. 9; Ms. 11. 71. (b) Full
of, filled with; दारिद्र्येणाभिभूतेन
त्वत्स्नेहानुगतेन च Mk. 4. 5;
वर्षधरकलमूकानुगतेन परिजनेन K. 159 consisting or
made up of; चिंतानुगतसर्वात्मन् Mb.
(c) Covered, as by a dress hanging
behind; शिवमिवानुगतं गजचर्मणा
Ki. 5. 2 (पश्चाद्व्याप्तं). (d) Extinguished
&c. (e) Acquired, obtained.
--2 (Used
actively) (a) Following, obeying,
observing; स्वमतमनुगतः Mu. 5. 19;
विभवानुगता भार्या Mk. 3. 28;
दिग्विजयप्रसंगेनानुगतो भूमिमिमां K. 191 come to;
Ms. 9. 267; K. 166; Mu. 6. 5; H. 2. 56;
R. 15. 9. (b) Corresponding or
tallying with, adapted or answering
to, in harmony with; सूत्रेणानुगतं भवति
Ś. B.; पादन्यासो लयमनुगतः M. 2. 9 in
accompaniment to the musical time;
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">Page0069-a+ 56</a>]
मृदंग ˚तः संगीतमधुरः Ratn. 1; ˚वीणैः
Śi. 11. 10. (c) Adequate or suitable to,
fit for; प्रस्तावानुगतं पृष्टः Pt. 5. (d)
Imitating; परितुष्टोऽस्मि यत्पितरमनुगतो
वत्सः M. 5 I am glad that the boy
takes after his father.
--तं Moderate
time in music.
--Comp.
--अर्थ a.
having a corresponding or easily
discoverable sense.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

