अनुत्तम|अनुत्तमः
अनुत्तम a. [न उत्तमो यस्मात्]
1
Than which there is nothing better,
having no superior or better,
unsurpassed, the very best or
highest, incomparably or pre-eminently
the best; सर्वद्रव्येषु विद्यैव
द्रव्यमाहुरनुत्तमं H. Pr. 4; कांक्षन् गतिमनुत्तमां
Ms. 2. 242; Y. 1. 87; अदस्त्वया
नुन्नमनुत्तमं तमः Śi. 1. 27 all-pervading;
Bg. 7. 18; Ms. 2. 9; 5. 158; 8. 81.
--2 Not the best.
--3 (In gram.)
Not used in the उत्तम or first,
person.
--मः N. of Śiva or Viṣṇu.
--Comp.
--अंभस्, --अंभसिकं a term in
Sāṃkhya philosophy, said to mean
‘indifference to and abstinence from
sensual enjoyment, as fatiguing
or involving injury to external
objects.’
