<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभवः|अनुभव
अनुभवः
1 Direct perception or
cognition, knowledge derived from
personal observation or experiment,
notion, apprehension, the impression
on the mind not derived from
memory, one of the kinds of
knowledge; सर्वव्यवहारहेतुर्ज्ञानं बुद्धिः । सा द्विविधा
स्मृतिरनुभवश्च । संस्कारमात्रजन्यं ज्ञानं स्मृतिः ।
तद्भिन्नं ज्ञानमनुभवः which again is
यथार्थ right & अयथार्थ wrong. See
T. S. 34. (The Naiyāyikas recognize
प्रत्यक्ष, अनुमान, उपमान and शाब्द as
the four sources of knowledge;
the Vedāntins and Mīmāṃsakas
add two more अर्थापत्ति and
अनुपलब्धि; the Vaiśeṣikas and Bauddhas
admit the first two only, the
Sāṃkhyas exclude उपमा, while the
Cārvākas admit प्रत्यक्ष only. Other
sections of philosophical schools
add three more to the six sources
of knowledge recognised by the
Mīmāṃsakas;
--संभव ‘equivalence’;
ऐतिह्य ‘fallible testimony’, and चेष्टा
‘gesture’.)
--2 Experience; अनुभवं
वचसा सखि लुंपसि N. 4. 105
--3
Understanding.
--4 Result, consequence.
--Comp.
--सिद्ध a. established by
experience.
