अनुराध|अनुराधः
अनुराध a.
1 Causing welfare; also
written as अनूराध; इंद्रं वयमनूराधं हवामहे
Av.
--2 Born under the asterism
अनुराधा P. IV. 3. 34.
--धा [अनुगता राधां
विशाखां] N. of the 17th of the 27 lunar
mansions or asterisms (so called
because it follows राधा or विशाखा). It
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-a" target="_blank">Page0079-a+ 57</a>]
consists of four stars.
--Comp.
--ग्रामः,
--पुरं the ancient capital of Laṅkā or
Ceylon; also called अनुरोधपुर,
described by Rājaśekhara as full of
curiosities. It is a large town in the north
of Ceylon “with 1600 square granite
pillars which supported the floor of
an enormous monastery called ‘The
Great Brazen Palace’ said to have
been built in 161 B. C.”
