अनुवाद्य
अनुवाद्य pot. p.
1 To be explained
or illustrated.
--2 (In gram.) To be
made the subject of an assertion (in a
sentence), opposed to विधेय which
affirms or denies something about
the subject. In a sentence the
अनुवाद्य or subject which is supposed to
be already known is repeated to
mark its connection with the विधेय or
predicate and should be placed first;
अनुवाद्यमनुक्त्वैव न विधेयमुदीरयेत्; in
वृद्धिरादैच् आदैच् should have been
placed first, though the
construction is defended by Patañjali.
