अनुशासनं|अनुशासन
अनुशासनं Advice, persuasion,
direction, order, command;
instruction, laying down rules or precepts;
a law, rule, precept; treatment (of
a subject), (with the object in
comp. or with gen., the agent, if
expressed, being put in the instr. or
gen.); भवत्यधिक्षेप इवानुशासनं
Ki. 1. 28 words of advice; तन्मनोरनुशासनं
Ms. 8. 139; 6. 50; 2. 159; यौवन˚ K. 146;
नामलिंग˚ laying down rules on the
gender of nouns, explanation of
gender &c.; शब्दानुशासनं Sk.;
शब्दानामनुशासनमाचार्यस्य आचार्येण वा
P. II. 3. 66 Sk.
--Comp.
--पर a.
obedient.
--पर्वन् N. of the 13th book
of the Mahābhārata (so called
because it lays down precepts of
advice).
