अंधस्|अन्धस्
अंधस् n. [अद्-असुन् नुम् धश्च;
अदेर्नुम्धौ च Uṇ. 4. 205] Food; द्विजातिशेषेण
यदेतदंधसा Ki. 1. 39; सशेष एवांधसि
असावतृप्यत् Dk. 133, 157 (supposed
to have in the Veda the senses of
Soma, the herb itself, or its juice,
juice, ghee or boiled rice, but usually
taken to mean ‘food’ only by
Indian lexicographers and
commentators). [cf. Gr. andhos].
