अपथ|अपथं|अपथः
अपथ a. [नास्ति पंथा यत्र] Pathless,
roadless; ˚थो देशः, ˚था नगरी &c.
--थं,
--थः (also अपंथाः P. V. 4. 72, II. {4}
II. 4. 30)
1 Not a way, absence of a way
or road, pathless state; a bad or
wrong road (lit.); (fig.)
irregularity, deviation, a moral irregularity
or deviation, a wrong road, bad or
evil course; अपथे पदमर्पयंति हि
श्रुतवंतोपि रजोनिमीलिताः R. 9. 74; 17. 54; न
कश्चिद्वर्णानामपथमपकृष्टोपि भजते Ś. 5. 10
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">Page0106-c+ 57</a>]
follows evil ways; कारितस्त्वमपथे पद
मया Ki. 13. 45, 64.
--2 Heresy,
heterodoxy (in opinions).
--3 The vulva.
--था N. of several plants.
--थं ind. By
or in the wrong way, astray; अपथं
वर्तते Sk.
--Comp.
--गामिन् a. pursuing
evil courses; heretical.
--प्रपन्न a.
taking to evil ways (as man); spent or
used out of place, misapplied,
misspent (as money &c.); H. 3. 123.
