अपविद्ध|अपविद्धः
अपविद्ध p. p.
1 Cast or thrown off,
thrown or cast away, abandoned,
forsaken, dismissed, rejected,
neglected, removed; oft. used in the
sense of ‘freed from,’ ‘devoid of’;
रक्षोविप्रकृतावास्तामपविद्धशुचाविव R. 10. 74.
--2 Abject, mean.
--द्धः, ˚पुत्रः A son that
is abandoned by the father or mother
or by both, and adopted by a stranger;
one of the 12 kinds of sons among
Hindus; Ms. 9. 171; Y. 2. 132.
--Comp.
--लोक a. dead, departed
from this world.
