अपस्
अपस् n. [आप् असुन् थस्वश्च;
आपःकर्माख्यायां थस्वो नुट्च वा स्यात् Uṇ. 4. 207.
अप्नः, अपः]
1 Work, action; अपसा
संतु नेमे Rv. 1. 54. 8.
--2 Sacred act
or rite, sacrificial work.
--3 Water.
--a. (अपाः)
1 Active, engaged in
any act (कर्मयुक्त).
--2 Got or
obtained. According to B. and R. अपसः
f. pl. stands in the Veda for (1)
the hands and fingers busy in
kindling the sacred fire and performing
the sacrificial rites; (2) the three
goddesses of sacred speech or the
three divinities, fire, wind and sun;
and (3) the active or running
waters. [cf. L. opus.]
