अपांग|अपाङ्ग|अपाङ्गः
अपांग --गक a. [अपगतं अंगं यस्य]
1 Wanting or deformed in some limb
of the body.
--2 Maimed, crippled.
--गः, --गकः [अपांगति तिर्यक् चलति नेत्रं
यत्र, अप-अंग्-घञ्]
1 The outer corner
or angle of the eye; चलापांगां दृष्टिं
Ś. 1. 24; अम्महे अपांगकः स्फुरति किमपि
वामकः M. 2. 4.
--2 A sectarial mark
on the forehead.
--3 Cupid, the god
of love.
--4 N. of a plant (अपामार्ग).
--Comp.
--दर्शनं, --दृष्टिः f.,
--विलोकितं,
--वीक्षणं &c. a side-glance, side-long
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">Page0115-c+ 56</a>]
look, wink.
--देशः the place of the
corner of the eye; the corner itself.
--नेत्र a. (said of a lady) having
eyes with beautiful (or long) outer
corners; यदियं पुनरप्यपांगनेत्रा
परिवृत्तार्धमुखी मयाद्य दृष्टा V. 1. 17 (a better
interpretation would however be
‘with the eyes turned towards the
corners’ अपांगयोः प्रेरिते नेत्रे यया i. e.
casting side-long looks).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

