<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रस्तुत|अप्रस्तुतं
अप्रस्तुत a.
1 Unsuitable to the
time or subject, not to the point,
irrelevant.
--2 Absurd, nonsensical;
रे गोरंभ किमप्रस्तुतं लपसि Pt. 1.
--3
Accidental or extraneous.
--4 Not ready.
--Comp.
--प्रशंसा a figure of speech
which, by describing the अप्रस्तुत (what
is not the subject matter) conveys
a reference to the प्रस्तुत or
subjectmatter; अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा सा या सैव
प्रस्तुताश्रया K. P. 10. It is of 5 kinds:
--कार्ये
निमित्ते सामान्ये विशेषे प्रस्तुते सति । तदन्यस्य
वचस्तुल्ये तुल्यस्येति च पंचधा ॥ i. e. when
the subject matter is viewed (a) as
an effect, information of which is
conveyed by stating the cause; (b)
when viewed as a cause by stating
the effect; (c) when viewed as a
general assertion by stating a
particular instance; (d) when viewed
as a particular instance by stating
a general assertion; and (e) when
viewed as similar by stating what is
similar to it, see K. P. 10; and
S. D. 706 for examples.
