अभिगम्
अभिगम् {c1c} P.
1 To go to, go near
to, approach (with acc.);
एनमभिजग्मुर्महर्षयः R. 15. 59; Ki. 10. 21;
मनुमेकाग्रमासीनमभिगम्य महर्षयः Ms. 1. 1;
11. 100.
--2 To follow, go after;
अनुरागाद्वने रामं दिष्ट्या त्वमभिगच्छसि
Rām.
--3 To find, meet with
(casually or by chance).
--4 To
cohabit, have sexual intercourse (with
man or woman); अभिगंतास्मि भगिनीं
मातरं वा तवेति ह Y. 2. 205; अभ्यगच्छः
पतिं यत्त्वं भजमानं Mb.
--5 To take to,
undertake, betake oneself to.
--6
To get, to share in; be subject to;
निद्रामभिगतः Rām.
--7 To conceive,
apprehend, understand,
comprehend. --Caus.
1 To cause to go to
or approach; take, convey, send;
Dk. 102.
--2 To cause to
apprehend; explain, teach.
