अभिमानः|अभिमान
अभिमानः
1 Pride(in a good sense),
self-respect, honourable or worthy
feeling; सदाभिमानैकधना हि मानिनः
Śi. 1. 67; Bh. 3. 5; अभिमानधनस्य
गत्वरैः Ki. 2. 19;
संकल्पयोनेरभिमानभूतं Ku. 3. 24.
--2 Self-conceit,
pride, arrogance, haughtiness,
egotism, high-opinion of oneself;
शिथिल˚नाः संवृत्ताः M. 2, Bh. 3. 46,
Bg. 16. 4; ˚वत् proud, conceited.
--3
Referring all objects to self, the act of
अहंकार, personality, misconception
(मिथ्याज्ञानं), see अहंकार.
--4 Conceit,
conception; supposition, belief,
opinion; Ki. 13. 7.
--5 Knowledge,
consciousness (बुद्धि, ज्ञान);
साधारण्याभिमानतः S. D.
--6 Affection, love.
--7 Desire, wishing for.
--8 Laying
claim to.
--9 Injury, killing,
seeking to injure.
--10 A sort of state
occasioned by love.
--Comp.
--शालिन् a. proud
--शून्य a. void of pride
or arrogance, humble.
