अभिषिच्
अभिषिच् {c6c} U. [˚सिच्, स् changed
to ष् by P. VIII. 3. 65]
1 To sprinkle,
pour down upon, water, wet,
shower upon (fig. also);
स्नातीहाभ्यषिचज्जलैः Bk. 6. 21; 15. 3; 6. 23;
संगे पुनर्बहुतराममृताभिषिक्तां Ch. P. 29
v. l.; अथ वपुरभिषेक्तुं तास्तदांभोभिरीषुः
Śi. 7. 75.
--2 To anoint, consecrate, appoint
&c. (by sprinkling water on the
head); to crown, install, inaugurate
(with loc. of the post of authority);
अग्निवर्णमभिषिच्य राघवः स्वे पदे
R. 19. 1, 17. 13; सोऽटवीराज्येऽभिषिक्तः
H. 2; V. 5. 23. --Caus.
1 To have
another consecrated, inaugurated
&c.
--2 To let oneself be crowned.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेकः|अभिषेक
अभिषेकः
1 Sprinkling, watering,
wetting.
--2 Anointing, inaugurating
or consecrating by sprinkling water
(a king, idol &c.).
--3 (Particularly)
Coronation, inauguration,
installation (of kings); royal unction;
अथाभिषेकं रघुवंशकेतोः R. 14. 7.
--4
The (holy) water required at
inauguration, coronation water;
अमात्यपरिषदं ब्रूहि संभ्रियतामायुषो
राज्याभिषेक इति V. 5; यौवराज्य˚ ibid.;
R. 17. 14.
--5 Bathing; ablution,
holy or religious bathing;
अभिषेकोत्तीर्णाय काश्यपाय Ś. 4;
अत्राभिषेकाय तपोधनानां R. 13. 51, 1. 85,
10. 63, 13. 58, 14. 82; K. 22, 36,
96; Ku. 5. 16; 7. 11; Ś. 7. 12;
H. 4. 87.
--6 Bathing or sprinkling
with water (of a divinity to whom
worship is offered).
--Comp.
--अहः
day of coronation.
--शाला
coronation-hall.
