अभीक|अभीकः
अभीक a. [For ety. see अभिक]
1 Longing after, desirous,
anxious.
--2 Lustful, libidinous,
voluptuous; मेदस्विनः सरभसोपगतानभीकान्
Śi. 5. 64.
--3 Fearless.
--4 Gone
to (अभिगत).
--5 Dreadful.
--कः
1 A
lover, husband.
--2 A poet.
--3 A
master.
--कं Ved.
1 Proximity,
nearness.
--2 Collision; combat,
encounter, opposition. The form अभीके
frequently occurs in the Vedas in
the sense of (a) near; (b) at the same
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">Page0142-c+ 55</a>]
time or place, at the right time, just
in time; (c) in a moment,
instantaneously, or (used like a
preposition with abl.), (d) from, out of; (e)
on account of, with regard to; (f.)
from.
