अमत|अमतः
अमत a.
1 Not felt, not
perceptible by the mind, unknown.
--2
Disliked, not agreed to, see under
अम् also.
--Comp.
--परार्थता ‘an
unaccepted second sense’, one of
the faults of a word (शब्ददोष); अमतः
प्रकृतविरुद्धः परार्थो यत्र; e. g. in
राममन्मथशरेण ताडिता &c. (R. 11. 20) the
second sense suggestive of शृंगाररस
is opposed to the proper rasa of
the passage which is either वीर or
बीभत्स; K. P. 7.
