accompanied by the use of spells or
incantations, as a cure &c.; अनया
कथमन्यथावलीढा न हि जीवंति जना मनागमंत्राः
Bv. 1. 111.
--Comp.
--तंत्र a.
without the use of spells or the
magical feats attendant on them,
without the use of magical arts; Pt. 1. 70.
--विद् a. Not knowing Vedic hymns.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमंद|अमन्द|अमन्दः
अमंद a.
1 Not slow or dull, active,
intelligent; M. 2. 8.
--2 Sharp,
strong, violent (wind &c.).
--3 Not
little, much, excessive, great,
violent; अमंदमददुर्दिन U. 5. 5;
अमंदमिलदिंदिरे निखिलमाधुरीमंदिरे Bv. 4. 1;
˚दष्टौष्ठकरावधूननं Ki. 8. 6 violently bit.
--दः
N. of a tree.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्यमान
अमन्यमान a. Ved.
1 Not
understanding; offering no homage.
--2 Not
being aware of.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्युत
अमन्युत a. Ved. Not bearing
illwill towards another.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमम|अममः
अमम a. Without egotism,
without any selfish or worldly
attachment, devoid of personal ties or de.
sires; शरणेष्वममश्चैव वृक्षमूलनिकेतनः
Ms. 6. 26.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
