अमोघ|अमोघः
अमोघ a.
1 Unfailing, reaching
the mark; धनुष्यमोघं समधत्त बाणं
Ku. 3. 66; R. 3. 53; 12. 97;
कामिलक्ष्येष्वमोधैः Me. 73.
--2 Unerring,
infallible (words, boon &c.); अमोधाः
प्रतिगृह्णंतावर्घ्यानुपदमाशिषः R. 1. 44;
युतममोघतया Ki. 6. 40.
--3 Not vain
or useless, efficacious, fruitful,
productive; यदमोघमपामंतरुप्तं बीजमज त्वया
Ku. 2. 5; so ˚बलं, ˚शक्ति, ˚वीर्य,
˚क्रोध &c.
--घः
1 Not failing or
erring, unerringness.
--2 N. of Viṣṇu
(or of Śiva according to some).
--3 N. of a river.
--घा
1 N.
of the plant पाटलां (Mar. पाडळी)
(the trumpet flower).
--2 N. of
another plant विडंग (Mar.
वावडिंग) the seed of which is used as a
vermifuge, and hence also called
कृमिघ्न.
--3 = पथ्या.
--4 N. of a spear or
शक्ति.
--5 N. of Śiva's wife.
--6
Mystical name of the conjunct consonant
क्ष.
--Comp.
--दंडः unerring in
punishment, N. of Śiva.
--दर्शिन्, --दृष्टि a. of
unerring mind or view.
--बल a. of
never-failing strength or vigour.
--वाच् f. words not vain or idle, that
are sure to be fulfilled or realized. (a.)
one whose words are not vain.
--वांछित a. never disappointed.
--विक्रमः
of never-failing valour, N. of Śiva.
