अरणिः|अरणि
अरणिः m. f.,
--णी f. [ऋ-अनि
Uṇ. 2. 101; अरणिः अग्नेर्योनिः] A piece of
wood (of the Śamī tree) used for
kindling the sacred fire by
attrition, the fire-producing wooden
stick; cf. Pt. 1. 216.
--णी (dual)
The two pieces of wood used
in kindling the sacred fire.
--णिः
1 The sun.
--2 Fire.
--3 Flint.
--4 N. of several fire-producing
plants, particularly अग्निमंथ.
--णिः f.
1 A path, way.
--2 Ved.
Stinginess.
--Comp.
--केतुः = अग्निमंथ
Premna Intergrifolia.
--सुतः N. of
Śuka, a celebrated sage (born from the
seed of Vyāsa fallen upon an Araṇi
at the sight of the nymph
Ghṛtāchī).
