अवंतिः|अवन्ति|अवंति|अवन्तिः
अवंतिः --ती f. [अव्-बाहु˚ झिच्
Uṇ. 3. 50]
1 N. of a city, the modern
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-c" target="_blank">Page0183-c+ 58</a>]
उज्जयिनी, one of the seven sacred cities of
the Hindus, to die at which is said to
secure eternal happiness; cf. अयोध्या
मथुरा माया काशी कांचिरवंतिका । पुरी
द्वारावती चैव सप्तैता मोक्षदायिकाः ॥. The women
of Avanti are said to be very
skilful in all erotic arts; cf. आवंत्य एव
निपुणा सुदृशो रतकर्मणि B. R. 10. 82.
--2
N. of a river. --m. pl. N. of a
country and its inhabitants; its
capital being उज्जयिनी on the river
सिप्रा; and there is also the temple
of महाकाल in the suburbs. [According to
Hemacandra अबंति is synonymous with
Mālava or the modern Mālavā; but the
latter country covered in ancient times,
as now, a wider area than Avanti, as
Bāṇa applies the name to a neighbouring
kingdom in the east, whose capital was
Vidiśā on the Vetravatī or Betvā. In
the time of the Mahābhārata Avanti
appears to have extended on the
south to the banks of the Narmadā
and on the west probably to the
banks of the Myhe or Mahi];
अवंतिनाथोऽयमुदग्रबाहुः R. 6. 32; असौ
महाकालनिकेतनस्य वसन्नदूरे किल
चंद्रमौलेः 6. 34, 35;
प्राप्यावंतीनुदयनकथाकोविदग्रामवृद्धान् Me. 30;
अवंतीषूज्जयिनी नाम नगरी K. 52.
--Comp.
--पुरं the city of Avanti
उज्जयिनी.
--ब्रह्मः [अवंतिषु ब्रह्मा अच् समासः
P. V. 4. 104] a Brāhmaṇa residing
in Avanti.
--सोमः [अवंतिषु सोम इव]
sour gruel prepared from the
fermentation of rice-water (कांजिकं).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

