1 The end or completion of a
principal sacrifice.
--2 Bathing at the
end of a principal sacrifice for
purification; नावभृथं सरस्वत्यां Kāty.;
भुवं कोष्णेन कुंडोध्नी मेध्येनावभृथादपि
R. 1. 84; प्रीत्याश्वमेधावभृथार्द्रमूर्तेः
6.; 9. 22; 11. 31; 13. 61; Y. 3. 244;
Ms. 11. 83.
--3 Purification by
bathing of the sacrificer and the
sacrificial vessels at the end of a
sacrifice.
--4 The water of purification.
--5 A supplementary sacrifice to
atone for defects in a principal and
preceding one; a sacrifice in general;
स्नातवत्यवभृथे ततस्त्वयि Śi. 14. 10.
--Comp.
--स्नानं ablution after a
sacrificial ceremony.
