आचार्यः|आचार्य|आचार्य्य|आचार्य्यः
आचार्यः [आ-चर्-ण्यत्
P. VI. 2. 36]
1 A teacher or preceptor (in
general).
--2 A spiritual guide
or preceptor, holy teacher (one
who invests a boy with the
sacred thread, instructs him in
the Vedas &c.); उपनीय तु यः शिष्यं
वेदमध्यापयेत् द्विजः । सकल्पं सरहस्यं च
तमाचार्यं प्रचक्षते Ms. 2. 140, see अध्यापक also.
--3 One who propounds a particular
doctrine.
--4 (When affixed to
proper names) Learned, venerable
(somewhat like the English Dr.).
--5
An adviser or preceptor at a
sacrifice &c.
--6 An epithet of Droṇa.
--र्या A female preceptor, a
spiritual preceptress.
--Comp.
--उपासनं
waiting upon or serving the
spiritual preceptor.
--करणं acting as a
teacher; P. I. 3. 36.
--देवः one
whose preceptor is his god.
--भोगीन
a. [आचार्यभोगाय हितं ख] to be enjoyed
by, fit for the use of, a preceptor;
delighting the preceptor.
--मिश्र a.
venerable, honourable.
