आदृ
आदृ {c6c} A. (द्रियते)
1 To respect,
honour, reverence; सीतां रघूत्तम
भवत्स्थितिमाद्रियस्व Mv. 7. 3 receive
respectfully; take or receive
respectfully; द्वितीयाद्रियते सदा H. Pr. 7;
सर्वे तस्यादृता धर्मा यस्यैते त्रय आदृताः
Ms. 2. 234; Bk. 6. 55.
--2 To
heed or care for, mind, take notice
of; usually with न; न त्यागमाद्रियते
K. 104, 167; वाक्यं नाद्रियते च
बांधवजनः Bh. 3. 111; अनादृत्य
disregarding; मम वचनमनादृत्य in spite
of or notwithstanding my words.
--3 To feel timid from a feeling of
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0238-b" target="_blank">Page0238-b+ 57</a>]
respect, be awed.
--4 To apply or
devote oneself closely to, have
regard for; भूरि श्रुतं शाश्वतमाद्रियंते
Māl. 1. 5.
--5 To desire, be eager for;
Mv. 6. 3.
--6 To enjoy honour, be
honoured.
