आपत्
आपत् {c1c} P.
1 To fall upon,
attack, assail; उदायुधानापततः
R. 12. 44, 5. 50; Bk. 3. 48.
--2 To
approach, come towards; K. 202;
एतत्प्रायेण श्रुतिविषयमापतितमेव K. 136
has reached the ears; 268.
--3 To
fly towards, come in flying, come or
drive in haste, rush upon.
--4 (a)
To happen, take place, occur, come
to pass; कथमिदमापतितं U. 2;
K. 262, 158; अहो न शोभनमापतितं Pt. 2.
(b) To fall to one's lot or share,
befall; अहोऽस्माकं महद्भोजममापतितं
Pt. 1; आपतंति हि
संसारपथमवतीर्णानामेते वृत्तांताः K. 175, 132; सर्वस्यैव
स्खलितमापतति 291; H. 1. 30, 173.
--5
(a) To occur to, cross (the mind);
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">Page0244-b+ 57</a>]
इति हृदये नापतितं K. 288. (b) To be
felt or regarded; मधुरतराण्यापतंति
मतसः K. 103 are felt or regarded;
202, 236, 329. --Caus. (पातयति)
To go towards, approach (Ved.).
