आशा
आशा [आसमंतात् अश्नुते आ-अश्-अच्]
1 (a) Hope, expectation, prospect;
तामाशां च सुरद्विषां R. 12. 96; आशा
हि परमं दुःखं नैराश्यं परमं सुखं Subhāṣ.;
त्वमाशे मोघाशे Bh. 3. 6; so भग्न, ˚हत,
˚निराश &c. (b) Wish, desire (in Bh. 3. 25
आशा is compared to a river).
--2
False hope or expectation.
--3 Space,
region, quarter of the compass,
direction;
अगस्त्याचरितामाशामनाशास्यजयो ययौ R. 4. 44;
Ki. 7. 9.
--Comp.
--अन्वित, --जनन a.
hopeful, inspiring hope; V. 3. 9.
--कृत a. attended with the hope of
success.
--गजः a guardian elephant
of a quarter or point of the compass;
see अष्टदिग्गज.
--तंतुः a thread of hope,
slender hope; Māl. 4. 3, 9. 26.
--पालः
a guardian or regent of the regions
or quarters; see अष्टदिक्पाल.
--पिशाचिका deceptive or illusive hope,
phantom of hope.
--पुरगुग्गुलुः or
--संभवः
a kind of Bdellium.
--प्राप्त a.
successful (= प्राप्ताश).
--बंधः {1} the tie or
bond of hope, confidence, trust,
expectation; गुर्वपि विरहदुःखमाशाबंधः
साहयति Ś. 4. 15; Ve. 6. 25; V. 3; U. 3;
Me. 10. {2} consolation. {3} a spider's
web.
--भंगः disappointment.
--वह
a. inspiring hope.
--(हः) N. of
a son of heaven.
--विभिन्न a.
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-a" target="_blank">Page0264-a+ 55</a>]
disappointed in expectation.
--हीन a.
despairing, despondent.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

