<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसः|आस
आसः [आस्-घञ्]
1 A seat.
--2 A
bow (--सं also); स सासिः सासुसूः
सासः Ki. 15. 5.
--3 Ashes.
--सं
1 Seat
or lower part of the body.
--2
Proximity.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसनं|आसन|आसनः
आसनं [आस्-ल्युट्]
1 Sitting down.
--2 A seat, place, stool; स
वासवेनासनसन्निकृष्टं Ku. 3. 2; आसनं मुच् to
leave one's seat, rise; R. 3. 11.
--3
A particular posture or mode of
sitting; cf. पद्म˚, वीर˚, भद्र˚, वज्र˚ &c.
--4 Sitting down or halting,
stopping, encamping.
--5 Abiding,
dwelling; Ms. 2. 245, 6. 59.
--6 Any
peculiar mode of sexual enjoyment
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">Page0267-c+ 57</a>]
(84 such asanas are usually
mentioned).
--7 Maintaining a post
against an enemy (opp. यानं), one
of the six modes of foreign policy;
which are: --संधिर्ना विग्रहो यानमासनं
द्वैधमाश्रयः Ak.; प्रतिबद्धशक्त्योः कालप्रतीक्षया
तूष्णीमवस्थानमासनं; परस्परस्य
सामर्थ्यविघातादासनं स्मृतं Agni P.; Ms. 7. 160,
162, 166; Y. 1. 346; Pt. 3.
--8 The
front part of an elephant's body,
withers.
--9 Throwing (fr. अस् to
throw).
--10 N. of two trees (असन and
जीवक).
--ना A seat, stool, stay.
--नी
1 Stay, abiding, sitting.
--2 A small
seat or stool.
--3 A shop, stall.
--Comp.
--बंधधीर a. resolute to sit
down, firm in one's seat;
निषेदुषीमासनबंधधीरः R. 2. 6.
