इद्
इद् ind.
1 A particle of
affirmation, even, just, only; especially in
strengthening a statement; अर्थज्ञ
इत्सकलं भद्रमश्नुते Nir.
--2 It is often
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-b" target="_blank">Page0276-b+ 56</a>]
added to words expressing excess
or exclusion; विश्व इत्, एक इत् &c.
--3
At the beginning of sentences it
often adds emphasis to pronouns,
prepositions &c. (Its place is taken
by एव in classical Sanskrit).
