उच्छ्वस्
उच्छ्वस् {c2c} P.
1 To breathe, live;
आस्मेच्छया न शक्यमुच्छ्वसितुमपि
K. 175; Ve. 5. 15; Ms. 3. 72;
अनुच्छ्वस्य without breathing, in one
breath.
--2 To take heart or courage,
cheer up, revive, breathe a sigh of
relief; नाद्याप्युच्छ्वसिति U. 3, 7;
त्वत्सन्निधावुच्छ्वसितीव चेतः Ki. 3. 8
is delighted; Śi. 18. 58; Ratn. 4;
दिगंतः Ki. 9. 21.
--3 To open,
bloom (as a lotus); नोच्छ्वसिति
तपनकिरणैः (कुमुदं) V. 3. 16;
M. 2. 11; Śi. 10. 58, 11. 15.
--4 To take
a deep breath, pant, sigh deeply;
Bk. 6. 120, 14. 55.
--5 To throb,
heave, palpitate.
--6 To be
loosened or relaxed. --Caus.
1 To cause to
breathe.
--2 To console, cheer up,
delight; Rs. 6. 8; U. 3; Śi. 9. 34.
--3
To loosen, relax, disjoin; Me. 58.
