out, expanded, dilated;
उत्तानतारक्रस्य लोचनयुगलस्य K. 143; U. 3. 23.
--2 (a) Lying on the back, with
the face upwards, supine;
Māl. 3; उत्तानोच्छूनमंडूकपाटितोदरसंनिभे
K. P. 7; Y. 1. 248. (b) Upright,
erect.
--3 Open, turned upwards;
उत्तानपाणिद्वयसंनिवेशात् Ku. 3. 45;
˚रशिमषु Pt. 3. 150.
--4 Open,
unreserved, frank, candid;
स्वभावोत्तानहृदयं Ś. 5 frank-minded.
--5
Elevated; Māl. 7.
--6 Concave;
having the mouth upwards.
--7 Shallow.
--Comp.
--कर्मकं a particular
posture in sitting.
--पत्रकः a species
of Ricinus (रक्तैरंड).
--पद् f.
vegetation, the whole creation of
upwardgerminating plants (Sāy.).
--पाद
a. with extended legs (children).
--(दः) {1} N. of a king, father of
Dhruva. {2} the Supreme Spirit. ˚जः
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">Page0293-a+ 56</a>]
N. of Dhruva, the polar star.
--शय a. sleeping supinely or on
the back, lying with the face
upwards; कदा उत्तानशयः पुत्रकः
जनयिष्यति मे हृदयाह्लादं K. 62.
--(यः, --या) a
little child, suckling, infant.
--शीवन्
a. lying extended; stagnant.
--हस्त
a. having the hands stretched out
in prayers.
--(स्तौ) (du.) the two
hands with the fingers stretched
out and with the backs turned
towards the ground.
