उत्थान|उत्थानं
उत्थान a. Causing to arise or
spring up.
--नं
1 The act of rising or
standing up, getting up; शनैर्यष्ट्युत्थानं
Bh. 3. 9.
--2 Rising (as of
luminaries); इंदुं नवोत्थानमिवेंदुमत्यै R. 6. 31
newly risen.
--3 Rise, origin.
--4
Resurrection.
--5 (a) Effort, exertion,
activity; मेदश्छेदकृशोदरं लघु
भवत्युत्थानयोग्यं वपुः Ś. 2. 5; ˚शीलः Dk. 153
disposed to work; Mv. 6. 23; यद्युत्थानं
भवेत्सह Ms. 9. 215, effort (for money),
acquisition of property. (b) Manly
exertion, manhood.
--6 Energy.
--7
Joy, pleasure.
--8 War, battle.
--9 An
army.
--10 Evacuating (by stool &c.).
--11 A book.
--12 A court yard.
--13
A shed where sacrifices are offered.
--14 A term, limit, boundary.
--15
Business (cares &c.) of a family or
realm.
--16 Reflection.
--17 Proximate
cause of a disease.
--18 Awakening.
--Comp.
--एकादशी the eleventh day
in the light fortnight of Kārttika
when Viṣṇu rises from his four
months' sleep (also called प्रबोधिनी).
