उपनम्
उपनम् {c1c} P.
1 To come to, arrive
at, approach, bend or tend towards.
--2 To befall, fall to the lot of,
occur, happen (used by itself or
with gen., dat., or acc. of person);
मत्संभोगः कथमुपनमेत् स्वप्नजोऽपि
Me. 91; तत्तस्योपनमेत् Bh. 2. 121; अंध
आत्मने नोपनमति Bhāg.; अपैनं सहस्रं
नमति Ait. Br.
--3 To share in. --Caus.
1 To lead towards, introduce (with
gen.).
--2 To offer, give.
