उपनत|उपनतः
उपनत p. p.
1 (a) Come near,
brought, arrived, approached,
brought near to; Ś. 5. 19; R. 12. 102.
(b) Got, obtained; अचिरोपनतां स
मेदिनीं R. 8. 7, 5. 52; चिंतितोपनतां
K. 129; V. 3. 22; V. 2.
--2 Presenting
itself, fallen to the lot of, befallen,
occurred; कस्यात्यंतं सुखमुपनतं
दुःखमेकांततो वा Me. 109; यदेवोपनतं
दुःखात्सुखं तद्रसवत्तरं V. 3. 21;
अनुपनतमनोरथस्य 22; 4. 3; so सुहृदुपनतः
Me. 100; Māl. 10; K. 33, 132, 348;
सुख˚ that readily or without
efforts presented itself Ś. 3;
अकामोपनतं R. 10. 39 unconsciously
committed.
--3 Formed, brought about,
effected.
--4 Presented to, offered,
given; परलोकोपनतं जलांजलिं
R. 8. 68.
--5 Bent down, humbled,
subjected, surrendered; दंडोपनतचरितं
R. 17. 81, 8. 81; दंडोपनतं शत्रुं Mb.
--6 Dependent on (for protection).
--7 Approximate, near (in time or
space.)
