ऋक्षः|ऋक्ष|ऋक्षं
ऋक्षः [ऋष्-स किच्च Uṇ. 3. 66]
1 A bear; Ms. 12. 67.
--2 N. of
a mountain.
--3 N. of a plant
(भल्लक).
--क्षः, --क्षं
1 A star,
constellation, lunar mansion; Ms. 2. 101;
3. 9; 6. 10.
--2 A sign of the zodiac.
--3 A star under which a man
happens to be born.
--क्षाः (m. pl.)
The seven stars called Pleiades;
afterwards the seven Ṛṣis;
R. 12. 25.
--क्षा The north.
--क्षी A female
bear. [cf. Gr. arkos; L. ursus].
--Comp.
--गंधा the plant Argyreia
Argentea (जांगली, महाश्वेता, क्षीरविदारी).
--गंधिका the plant Batatas
Paniculata.
--चक्रं the circle of stars.
--नाथः, --ईशः ‘lord of stars,’ the
moon.
--नेमिः N. of Viṣṇu.
--राज्,
--जः {1} the moon. {2} Jāmbuvat,
the king of bears.
--हरीश्वरः the lord
of bears and apes; R. 13. 72.
