ऋच्
ऋच् f. [ऋच्यते स्तूयतेऽनया, ऋच्
करणे क्विप्]
1 A hymn (in general).
--2
A single verse, stanza, or text; a
verse of the Ṛgveda (opp. यजुस् and
सामन्); त्रेधा विहिता वागृचो यजूंषि
सामानि Śat. Br.
--3 The collective body
of the Ṛgveda (pl.); ऋचः सामानि
जज्ञिरे Rv. 10. 90. 9.
--4
Splendour (for. रुच्).
--5 Praise.
--6
Worship.
--Comp.
--अयनं [ऋचामयनं]
N. of a book; ऋक्पारायण; ˚आदि N.
of a collection of words in Pāṇini.
--आवानं the time for reciting the
Vedas.
--गाथा N. of a certain song.
--तंत्रं, --व्याकरणं N. of the
Pariśiṣṭas of the Sāma-veda.
--भाज् a.
partaking of a Ṛk, (as a deity
who is addressed with it).
--विधानं
the performance of certain rites
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0348-a" target="_blank">Page0348-a+ 58</a>]
by reciting verses of the Ṛg-veda.
--वेदः the oldest of the four
Vedas, and the most ancient
sacred book of the Hindus.
[The Ṛgveda is said to have been
produced from fire; cf. Ms. 1. 23. This
Veda is divided, according to one
arrangement, into 8 Aṣṭakas, each of
which is divided into as many Adhyāyas:
according to another arrangement into
10 Maṇḍalas, which are again
subdivided into 1000 Anuvākas, and
comprises 1000 sūktas. The total
number of verses or Ṛks is above 1000].
--संहिता the arranged collection of
the hymns of Ṛgveda.
--साम (˚मे
dual) the verses Ṛk and Sāman.
˚शृंगः N. of Viṣṇu.
