कटिः|कटि
कटिः, --टी f. [कट्-इन्]
1 The hip.
--2 The buttocks (considered by
rhetoricians as vulgar and
colloquial in these senses; the word कटि in
कटिस्ते हरते मनः is said to be ग्राम्य.)
--3 An elephant's cheek.
--टी
Long pepper.
--Comp.
--कूपः the
hollow above the hip, the loins.
--तटं the loins; कटीतटनिवेशितं
Mk. 1. 27.
--त्रं {1} a cloth girt round the
loins. {2} a zone, girdle. {3} an
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0369-c" target="_blank">Page0369-c+ 56</a>]
ornament of small bells worn round
the loins. {4} an armour of the hip or
the loins.
--देशः the loins. (--टि
or टी) प्रोथः the buttocks.
--मालिका
a woman's zone or girdle.
--रोहकः
the rider of an elephant (who sits
upon the hinder parts of the
elephant as distinct from the driver).
--शीर्षकः the loins.
--शृंखला a
girdle furnished with small bells.
--सूत्रं a zone or waistband.
