कलहः|कलह|कलहं
कलहः, --हं [कलं कामं हंति हण्-ड Tv.]
1 Strife, quarrel: ईर्ष्याकलहः Bh. 1. 2;
लीला˚ Ś. Til. 8; so शुष्ककलहः,
प्रणयकलहः &c.
--2 War, battle.
--3
Trick, deceit, falsehood.
--4 Violence,
kicking, beating &c; Ms. 4. 121;
(where Medhātithi and Kullūka
explain कलह by दडादिनेतरेतरताडनं and
दंडादंड्यादि respectively).
--5 A road,
way.
--6 The sheath of a sword.
--7
A cry, sound; Māl. 9. 18.
--Comp.
--अंतरिता a woman separated from
her lover in consequence of a
quarrel with him (one who is angry
and yet sorry for it); she is thus
defined in S. D.:
--चाटुकारमपि
प्राणनाथं रोषादपास्य या । पश्चात्तापमवाप्नोति
कलहांतरिता तु सा ॥ 117.
--अपहृत a. taken
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-c" target="_blank">Page0386-c+ 56</a>]
by main force or violence.
--कार,
--कारिन् a. quarrelsome, turbulent.
--प्रिय a. fond of (promoting)
quarrels; ननु कलहप्रियोसि M. 1.
--(यः) an epithet of Nārada.
--(या)
a bird (सारिका).
