कीचकः|कीचक
कीचकः [Uṇ. 5. 56]
1 A hollow
bamboo.
--2 A bamboo rattling or
whistling in the wind; शब्दायंते
मधुरमनिलैः कीचकाः पूर्यमाणाः Me. 56;
R. 2. 12; 4. 73; Ku. 1. 8.
--3 N. of a
people.
--4 N. of the
commander-inchief of king Virāṭa. [While
Draupadī in the guise of Sairandhrī was
residing at the court of king Virāṭa with
her five husbands also disguised,
Kīchaka once happened to see her, and her
beauty stirred up wicked passion in his
heart. He thenceforward kept a sinister
eye on her, and endeavoured through
the help of his sister, the king's wife, to
violate her chastity. Draupadī
complained of his unmannerly conduct
towards herself to the king; but when he
declined to interfere, she sought the
assistance of Bhīma, and at his
suggestion showed herself favourable to his
advances. It was then agreed that they
should meet at mid-night in the dancing
hall of the palace. Pursuant to
appointment Kīcaka went there and
attempted to embrace Draupadī (as he fancied
Bhīma to be owing to the darkness of
night). But the wretch was at once
seized and crushed to death by the
powerful Bhīma].
--Comp.
--जित् m.
an epithet of Bhīma, the second
Pāṇḍava prince.
