कुप्
कुप् {vI.v} {c4c} P. (कुप्यति, चुकोप, अकुपत्,
कोपितुं, कुपित)
1 To be angry,
(generally with the dat. of the
person who is the object of anger,
but sometimes with the acc. or
gen. also); कुप्यतिं हितवादिने
K. 108; कुपितश्चंद्रगुप्तश्चाणक्यस्योपरि Mu. 2;
M. 3. 21; U. 7; चुकोप तस्मै स भृशं
R. 3. 56.
--2 To be excited, to gather
strength, be virulent; as in दोषाः
प्रकुप्यंति Suśr. --Caus. (कोपयति-ते)
1
To provoke, irritate; to excite,
agitate.
--2 To stir up. {vII.v} {c10c} U.
1
To shine.
--2 To speak.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपः|कोप
कोपः [कुप्-भावे घञ्]
1 Anger,
wrath, passion; कोपं न गच्छति
नितांतबलोपि नागः Pt. 1. 123; न त्वया
कोपः कार्यः do not be angry.
--2 (In
medicine) Morbid irritation or
disorder of the humours of the
body; i. e. पित्तकोप, वातकोप. &c.
--Comp.
--आकुल, --आविष्ट a. enraged,
furious.
--क्रमः {1} an angry or passionate
man. {2} the course of anger.
--दीप्त,
--ज्वलित a. inflamed with anger.
--पदं {1} cause of anger. {2}
pretended anger.
--वशः subjection
to anger.
--वेगः violence, fury
of anger.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

