कुबेरः|कुबेर
कुबे(वे)रः [कुत्सितं बे(वे)रं शरीरं
यस्य सः] The god of riches and
treasure and the regent of the
northern quarter; कुबेरगुप्तां दिशमुष्णरश्मौ
गंतुं प्रवृत्ते समयं विलंघ्य Ku. 3. 25 (vide
Malli. thereon.). [Kubera is the son of
Viśravas by Iḍaviḍā and thus the
halfbrother of Rāvaṇa. Besides being the
lord of riches and regent of the north,
he is the king of the Yakṣas and
Kinnaras, and a friend of Rudra. His abode
is Kailāsa. He is represented as being
deformed in body-having three legs,
only eight teeth, and a yellow mark
in place of one eye].
--Comp.
--अद्रिः.
--अचलः an epithet of mountain
Kailāsa.
--दिश् f. the north.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0410-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

