कुब्ज|कुब्जः
कुब्ज a. [कु ईषत् उब्जमार्जंवं यत्र शकं˚
Tv.] Hump-backed, crooked.
--ब्जः
1
A curved sword.
--2 A hump on
the back.
--ब्जा A young female
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0410-b" target="_blank">Page0410-b+ 58</a>]
servant of Kaṃsa, said to be
deformed in three parts of her body.
[Kṛṣṇa and Balarāma, while
proceeding to Mathurā, saw her on the high
road carrying unguent to Kaṃsa. They
asked her if she would give them some
portion of it, and she gave as much as
they wanted. Kṛṣṇa, being very much
pleased with her kindness, made her
perfectly straight, and she began
to appear a most beautiful woman].
--Comp.
--किरातंः --वामनं a
hump-backed person and a dwarf.
--गामिन् a.
going crookedly, going astray;
Pt. 2. 5.
--लीला the manner, gait, or
character of a hump-backed person;
Ś. 2.
