1 What should or ought to be
done, right, proper, fit.
--2 Feasible,
practicable.
--3 Who may be
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0419-c" target="_blank">Page0419-c+ 55</a>]
seduced from allegiance, treacherous;
Rāj. T. 5. 247.
--त्यं
1 What ought
to be done, duty, function;
Ms. 2. 237; 7. 67.
--2 Work, business, deed,
commission; बंधुकृत्यं Me. 114;
अन्योन्यकृत्यैः Ś. 7. 34.
--3 Purpose,
object, end; कूजद्भिरापादितवंशकृत्यं
R. 2. 12; Ku. 4. 15.
--4 Motive, cause.
--त्यः A class of affixes used to
form potential (future) passive
participle; these are तव्य, अनीय, य and
also एलिम.
--त्या
1 Action, deed.
--2
Magic.
--3 A female deity to whom
sacrifices are offered for
destruetive and magical purposes.
