कृत्तिका
कृत्तिका (pl.) [कृत्-तिकन् किच्च;
Uṇ. 3. 147]
1 The third of the 27 lunar
mansions or asterisms, (consisting
of 6 stars) the Pleiades.
--2 The
six stars represented as nymphs
acting as nurses to Kārtikeya, the
god of war.
--Comp.
--अंजिः a kind
of horse in an Aśvamedha sacrifice
having a carriage as an emblem.
--तनयः, --पुत्रः, --सुतः epithets of
Kārtikeya.
--भवः the moon.
