क्षीण|क्षीणः
क्षीण p. p. [क्षि-क्त]
1 Thin,
emaciated, waned, become lean,
diminished, worn away, expended; भार्यां
क्षीणेषु वित्तेषु (जानीयात्) H. 1. 72; so क्षीणः.
शशी; क्षीणे पुण्ये मर्त्यलोके विशंति.
--2
Slender, delicate.
--3 Small, little.
--4 Poor, miserable.
--5 Powerless,
weak.
--6 Wasted away, decreased,
lost, diminished.
--7 Dead, destroyed;
अक्षीणभक्तिः क्षीणेऽपि नंदे Mu. 2. 21,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-a" target="_blank">Page0437-a+ 56</a>]
--8 Injured, broken, torn.
--Comp.
--चंद्रः the moon on the wane.
--धन
a. reduced to poverty,
impoverished.
--पाप a. one who is purified
after having suffered the
consequences of sin.
--पुण्य a. one who
has enjoyed all his stock of merit,
and must work to acquire more in
another birth.
--मध्य a.
slenderwaisted.
--वासिन् a. inhabiting a
dilapidated house. (m.) a dove or
pigeon.
--विक्रांत a. destitute of
courage or prowess.
--वृत्ति a.
deprived of the means of support, out of
employ.
--शक्ति, --बल a. weakened in
strength, subsided (as a disease);
Pt. 1. 235.
