ग्रंथिः|ग्रन्थि|ग्रंथि|ग्रन्थिः
ग्रंथिः
1 A knot, bunch,
protuberance in general; स्तनौ मांसग्रंथी
कनककलशावित्युपमितौ Bh. 3. 20; so मेदोग्रंथि.
--2 A tie or knot of a cord,
garment &c.; इदमुपहितसूक्ष्मग्रंथिना
स्कंधदेशे Ś. 1. 18; Mk. 1. 1;
Ms. 2. 43; Bh. 1. 57.
--3 A knot tied in
the end of a garment for keeping
money; hence, purse, money,
property; कुसीदाद् दारिद्र्यं
परकरगतग्रंथिशमनात् Pt. 1. 11.
--4 The joint or
knot of a reed, cane &c.
--5 A joint
of the body.
--6 Crookedness,
distortion, falsehood, perversion of
truth.
--7 Swelling and hardening
of the vessels of the body.
--Comp.
--छेदकः, --भेदः, --मोचकः a cut-purse,
a pick pocket; अंगुलीर्ग्रंथिभेदस्य छेदयेत्
प्रथमे ग्रहे Ms. 9. 277; Y. 2. 274;
Ś. 6.
--पर्णः, --र्णं {1} N. of a fragrant
tree; न ग्रंथिपर्णप्रणयाश्चरंति
कस्तूरिकागंधमृगास्तृणेषु Vikr. 1. 17. {2} a
kind of perfume.
--बंधनं {1} tying
together the garments of the bride
and the bridegroom at the
marriage ceremony. {2} tying a knot.
{3} a ligament.
--मूलं garlic.
--हरः
a minister.
