चरुः|चरु
चरुः [चर् उन्]
1 An oblation of
rice or barley boiled for presentation
to the gods and the manes:
अनवस्रावी निरुष्मपक्व आंदनश्चरुरिति याज्ञिकाः (It
is often boiled in milk and is called
पयश्चरु; cf. R. 10. 51, 54, 56; or
sprinkled over with butter or ghee.)
--2 A kind of vessel in which an
oblation is prepared.
--3 A cloud.
--Comp.
--चेलिन् m. N. of Śiva.
--स्थाली a
vessel for boiling rice &c for
presentation to the gods and the manes.
