but is used in one which is in some
way connected with the primary
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">Page0510-b+ 57</a>]
sense; e. g. in the familiar instance
गंगायां घोषः ‘a hamlet on the Ganges,’
गंगा loses its primary sense and
means गंगातट; cf. अजहत्स्वार्था also.
{2} irony.
