जाया
जाया A wife. (The word is
thus derived: --पतिर्भार्यां संप्रविश्य गर्भो
भूत्वेह जायते । जायायास्तद्धि जायात्वं
यदस्यां जायते पुनः Ms. 9. 8; see also
Malli. on R. 2. 1). As last
member of Bah. comp. जाया is changed
to जानि; सीताजानिः ‘one who has
Sītā for his wife’; so युवजानिः,
वामार्धजानिः.
--Comp.
--अनुजीविन्
m.,
--आजीवः {1} an actor, a dancer.
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-c" target="_blank">Page0512-c+ 57</a>]
{2} the husband of a harlot. {3} a
needy man, pauper. {4} a kind of
crane (बक).
--घ्नः {1} a murderer of
his wife. {2} a mole or mark on
the body indicative of the death of
one's wife.
--पती (dual)
husband and wife. (The other forms
of the comp. are दंपती and जंपती q. v.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

