जित|जितः
जित p. p. [जि-कर्मणि क्त]
1
Conquered, subdued, curbed, restrained,
(as enemies, passions &c.)
--2
Won, got, obtained (by conquest).
--3 Surpassed, excelled.
--4 Subject
to, enslaved or influenced by;
कामजित; स्त्रीजित &c.
--तं Victory.
--Comp.
--अक्षर a. reading well or
readily.
--अमित्र a. one who has
conquered his foes, triumphant,
victorious. {2} one who has subdued
his passions.
--(त्रः) N. of Viṣṇu.
--अरि a. one who has conquered
his enemies or passions.
--(रिः) an
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">Page0514-a+ 56</a>]
epithet of Buddha.
--आत्मन् a.
selfsubdued, void of passion.
--आहव
a. victorious.
--इंद्रिय a. one who
has conquered his passions or
subdued the senses (रूप, रस, गंध, स्पर्श
& शब्द); श्रुत्वा स्पष्ट्वाथ दृष्ट्वा च भुक्वा
घ्रात्वा च यो नरः । न हृष्यति ग्लायति
वा स विज्ञेयो जितेंद्रियः Ms. 2. 98.
--काशिः the fist doubled.
--काशिन्
a. appearing victorious, proud of
victory, assuming the airs of a
victor; चाणक्योऽपि जितकाशितया
Mu. 2; जितकाशी राजसेवकः ibid.
--कोप,
--क्रोध, --मन्यु a. imperturbable, not
excitable
--(धः) an epithet of
Viṣṇu.
--नेमिः a staff made of the
Aśvattha tree.
--लोक a. ‘one who has won
heaven’ (epithet of a class of manes).
--शत्रु a. victorious.
--श्रम a. inured
to fatigue, hardy.
--स्वर्ग a. one who
has won heaven.
