<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्ष्
तक्ष् a. (At the end of comp.)
Paring, cutting &c.; also तक्ष.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षकः|तक्षक
तक्षकः [तक्ष् ण्वुल्]
1 A carpenter,
wood-cutter (whether by caste or
profession).
--2 The chief actor in
the prelude of a drama (i. e. the
सूत्रधार).
--3 N. of the architect of the
gods.
--4 N. of one of the principal
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">Page0525-b+ 50</a>]
Nāgas or serpents of the Pātāla,
son of Kaśyapa and Kadru; (saved
at the intercession of the sage
Āstīka from being burnt down in the
serpent-sacrifice performed by king
Janamejaya, in which many others
of his race were burnt down to
ashes).
