तुलसी
तुलसी [तुलां सादृश्यं स्यति, सो-क
गौरा˚ ङीष् शकंध्वा. Tv.] The holy basil held
in veneration by the Hindus,
especially by the worshippers of Viṣṇu.
--Comp.
--पत्रं (lit.) a Tulasī leaf;
(fig.) a very small gift.
--विवाहः
the marriage of an image of
Bālakṛṣṇa with the holy basil,
performed on the 12th day of the bright
half of Kārtika.
--वृंदावनः --नं a square
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0543-a" target="_blank">Page0543-a+ 55</a>]
pedestal in which the sacred basil is
planted.
