दासः|दास
दासः
1 A slave, servant in
general; गृहकर्मदासाः Bh. 1. 1; गृह˚,
कर्म˚ &c.
--2 A fisherman.
--3 A
Śūdra, a man of the fourth caste.
--4
A knowing man, one who knows the
universal spirit.
--5 N. of Vṛtrāsura.
--6 A demon.
--7 A savage,
barbarian (opp. आर्य).
--8 A worthy
recipient (दानपात्र).
--9 A word added
to the name of a Śūdra; cf. गुप्त.
--Comp.
--अनुदासः ‘a slave of a
slave’, the humblest of the
servants; (sometimes used by the
speaker as a mark of humility).
--जनः a servant or slave;
कमपराधलवं मयि पश्यसि त्यजसि मानिनि
दासजनं यतः V. 4. 29; (दासस्यकुलं is
used as a compound in the sense
of ‘the mob or the common
people’).
--भावः servitude.
