<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासी
दासी
1 A female servant or slave.
--2 The wife of a fisherman.
--3
The wife of a Śūdra.
--4 An altar.
--5 A harlot.
--Comp.
--पुत्रः,
--सुतः the son of a female slave.
--श्रोत्रियः a Brāhmaṇa (knowing
the Vedas) attached to a female
slave.
--सभं a collection of female
slaves. (The gen. sing. दास्याः
enters into some compounds, but
loses its literal sense; e. g. दास्याःपुत्रः,
--सुतः ‘a whore-son’, used as a
term of abuse; दास्याःपुत्रैः
शकुनिलुब्धकैः Ś. 2; but दास्याः सदृशी ‘like
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-c" target="_blank">Page0564-c+ 54</a>]
a female slave’).
