दिव्
दिव्^1 {vI.v} {c4c} P. (दीव्यति, द्यूत or द्यून;
desid. दुद्यूषति, दिदेविषति)
1 To shine,
be bright.
--2 To throw, cast (as a
missile); Bk. 17. 87, 5. 81.
--3 To
gamble, play with dice (with acc
or instr. of the ‘dice’); अक्षैरक्षान्वा
दीव्यति Sk.; Śi. 8. 32; Ve. 1. 13.
--4
To play, sport.
--5 To joke, trifle
with, make sport of, rally; (with
acc.).
--6 To stake, make a bet.
--7
To sell. deal in (with gen.);
अदेवीद्वंधुभीगानां Bk. 8. 122; (but with
acc. or gen. when the root is
preceded by a preposition; शतं शतस्य
वा परिदीव्यति Sk.).
--8 To squander,
make light of.
--9 To praise.
--10 To
be glad, rejoice.
--11 To be mad or
drunk.
--12 To be sleepy.
--13 To
wish for. {vII.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (देवति,
देवयति-ते)
1 To cause to lament, pain,
vex, torment.
--2 To ask, beg. {vIII.v}
{c10c} A. (देवयते) To suffer pain, lament,
moan. --WITH परि to lament, moan,
suffer pain; Bk. 4. 34.
[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: verb missing virama.
