नम्
नम् {c1c} P., sometimes A. (नमति-ते,
ननाम, अनंसीत्, नंस्यति, नत; caus.
नमयति-ते or नामयति-ते, but with a
preposition नमयति only; desid. निनंसति)
1 To bow to, make obeisance to,
salute (as a mark of respect) (with
acc. or dat.); इयं नमति वः सर्वान्
त्रिलोचनवधूरिति Ku. 6. 89; Bg. 11. 37;
Bk. 9. 51, 10. 31; 12. 39;
Śi. 4. 57.
--2 To submit or subject oneself,
bow down; अशक्तः संधिमान् नमेत्
Kām. 8. 55.
--3 To bend, sink;
go down; अनंसीद्भूर्भरेणास्य Bk. 15. 25.
नेमुः सर्वदिशः K. 55; उन्नमति नमति
वर्षति…मेघः Mk. 5. 26.
--4 To stoop,
be inclined.
--5 To be bent or
curved.
--6 To sound.
--7 To change a
dental to a lingual letter. --Caus.
1 To bend, make curved.
--2 To
bend (as a bow); Ś. 2. 3.
--3
To cause to sink.
--4 To prevent,
ward off.
