नश्
नश् {vI.v} {c4c} P. (नश्पति, ननाश, अनशत्,
नंक्ष्यति, नशिष्यति नष्ट; caus. नाशयति; desid.
निनंक्षति, निनशिषति)
1 To be lost, to
disappear, vanish, become invisible;
ध्रुवाणि तस्य नश्यंति H. 1; तथा सीमा
न नश्यति Ms. 8. 247; Y. 2. 58;
क्षणनष्टदृष्टतिमिरं Mk. 5. 24.
--2 To be
destroyed, to perish, die, be ruined;
जीवनाशं ननाश च Bk. 14. 31;
Ms. 8. 166, 7. 40; Mu. 6. 8.
--3 To run
away, fly away, escape; नश्यंति
वृंदानि ददर्श कवींद्रः Bk. 10. 12; नेशुश्चित्रा
निशाचराः 14. 112; Ratn. 2. 3.
--4
To be frustrated, become unsuccess
ful. --Caus.
1 To cause to disappear.
--2 To destroy, remove, efface, drive
away, cause to fly away.
--3 To
violate, (as a virgin).
--4 To cause to
be lost, lose.
--5 To forget.
--6 To
extinguish, put out (as fire). {vII.v}
{c1c} U. (नशति-ते) Ved.
1 To reach,
attain.
--2 To meet with, find.
