नायक|नायकः
नायक a. [नी-ण्वुल्] Guiding,
leading, conducting.
--कः
1 A guide,
leader, conductor.
--2 A chief,
master, head, lord.
--3 A
pre-eminent or principal person,
distinguished personage; सैन्यनायकः &c.
--4 A general, commander.
--5 (In
Rhet.) The hero of a poetic
composition (a play or drama);
(according to S. D. there are four
main kinds of नायकः -- धीरोदात्त,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">Page0615-c+ 58</a>]
धीरोद्धत, धीरललित, and धीरप्रशांत, q. q. v. v;
these are again subdivided, the total
number of kinds being 48; see
S. D. 64-75. The Rasamañjarī mentions {3}
classes पति, उपपति and वैशिक;
95. 110).
--6 The central gem of a neck.
lace.
--7 A paradigm or leading
example; दशैते स्त्रीषु नायकाः.
--8 An
epithet of Śākyamuni.
--Comp.
--अधिपः a king, sovereign.
