निभृत|निभृतः
निभृत a.
1 Placed down,
deposited, lowered.
--2 Filled with, full
of; चिंतया निभृतः Bhāg.
--3
Concealed, hidden, out of sight,
unperceved, unobserved; निभृतो भूत्वा
Pt. 1; नभसा निभृतेंदुना R. 8. 15 ‘with
the moon become invisible, about
to set or go down’; Ve. 6. 2,
Śi. 6. 20.
--4 Secret, covert; Śi. 13. 42.
--5 (a) Still, silent; निभृतद्विरेफं (
काननं) Ku. 3. 42, 6. 2. (b) Steady,
fixed, immovable, motionless;
Ś. 1. 8.
--6 Mild, gentle; अनिभृता
वायवः Ki. 13. 66 ‘not gentle,
violent or strong’; Māl. 2. 12;
Mv. 3. 14.
--7 Modest, humble; अनिभृतकरेषु
प्रियेषु Me. 68; प्रणामनिभृता कुलवधूरिव
Mu. 1.
--8 Firm, resolute.
--9
Lonely, solitary; निभृतनिकुंजगृहं गतया
Gīt. 2.
--10 Shut, closed (as a door).
--11 True, faithful, firmly attached.
--तं Modesty, humility.
--तं ind.
1
Secretly, covertly, privatly,
unperceived; Ś. 3; Śi. 3. 74;
Ms. 9. 263.
--2 Silently, quietly; K. 134.
--3
Out of sight, in a corner.
--Comp.
--आत्मन् a. firm, resolute.
