निर्वेदः|निर्वेद|निर्व्वेदः
निर्वेदः
1 Disgust, loathing.
--2
Satiety, cloy.
--3 Depression of
spirits, despair, despondency;
परिभवान्निर्वेदमापद्यते Mk. 1. 14.
--4
Humiliation.
--5 Grief.
--6 Complete
indifference to worldly objects;
Bg. 2. 52 regarded as the feeling
which gives rise to the sentiment
called शांत (quietude);
निर्वेदस्थायिभावोस्ति शांतोऽपि नवमो रसः
K. P. 4; (see R. G. under निर्वेद).
--7
Selfdisparagement or humiliation
(regarded as one of the 33
subordinate feelings); cf. the definition in
R. G. under निर्वेद; (the following
is there given as an instance; यदि
लक्ष्पण सा मृगेक्षणा न मदीक्षासरणिं समेष्यति ।
अमुना जडजीवितेन मे जगता वा विफलेन किं
फलं ॥).
--8 Shame.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विश्
निर्विश् {c6c} P.
1 To enjoy;
ज्योत्स्नावतो निर्विशति प्रदोषान् R. 6. 34;
निर्विष्ठविषयस्नैहः स दशांतमुपेयिवान्
R. 12. 1; 4. 51; 6. 50; 9. 36; 13. 60;
14. 80; 18. 3; 19. 47; Me. 110;
Ku. 1. 29.
--2 To adorn, embellish.
--3 To marry; निर्वेष्टुकामोस्मि नरेंद्र
V. P.
--4 To feel, experience.
--5 To
reward, recompense.
