नीच|नीचः
नीच a. [निकृष्टतमीं शोभां चिनोति, चि-ड
Tv.]
1 Low, short, small, little,
dwarfish.
--2 Situated below, being
in a low position; Bg. 6. 11;
Ms. 2. 198; Y. 1. 131.
--3 Lowered, deep
(as a voice).
--4 Low, mean, base,
vile, worst; प्रारभ्यते न खलु विघ्नभयेन
नीचैः Bh. 2. 27; नीचस्य गोचरगतैः
सुखमास्यते कैः 59; Bv. 1. 48.
--5
Worthless, insignificant.
--चा An
excellent cow.
--चं The lowest point
of a planet.
--Comp.
--उक्तिः f. a low
or vulgar expression.
--उच्चवृत्तं an
epicycle.
--उपगत a. situated low in
the sky.
--ग a. {1} going
downwards, descending (as a river). {2}
low, base, vile.
--(गा) a river.
--(गं)
water.
--गृहं (in astr.) the part of
the heavens in which a planet stands
at its lower point.
--भोज्यः onion.
--योनिन् a. of low origin, low-born;
so नीचजाति.
--वज्रः, --ज्रं a kind of
gem (वैक्रांत).
