नीविः|नीवि
नीविः, --वी f. [निव्ययति निवीयते वा
निव्ये-इन्; cf. Uṇ. 4. 135]
1 A cloth
worn round a woman's waist, or
more properly the ends of the cloth
tied into a knot in front, the knot
of the wearing garment;
प्रस्थानभिन्नां न बबंध नीविं R. 7. 9;
नीविबंधोच्छ्वसनं Māl. 2. 5; Ku. 1. 38; नीवि
प्रति प्रणिहिते तु करे प्रियेण K. P. 4;
Me. 68; Śi. 10. 64.
--2 The outer tie
of a packet in which the offerings
of a Śūdra at funeral obsequies are
presented.
--3 Capital, principal,
stock.
--4 A stake, wager.
