परिजल्पितं|परिजल्पित
परिजल्पितं A covert indication
(as by a servant) of one's own
skill, superiority &c. by pointing
out the cruelty, deceitfulness and
such other faults of his master;
Ujjvalamaṇi thus defines it:
--प्रभोर्निर्दयताशाठ्यचापलाघुपपादनात् ।
स्वविचणताव्यक्तिर्भंग्या स्यात्परिजल्पितम् ॥ (Wilson
renders the word by ‘the covert
reproaches of a mistress neglected
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">Page0674-b+ 56</a>]
or ill-used by her lover’).
