परिवृत्तिः|परिवृत्ति
परिवृत्तिः f.
1 Revolution;
Śi. 10. 91.
--2 Return; turning back.
--3
Barter, exchange.
--4 End,
termination.
--5 Surrounding.
--6 Staying
or dwelling in a place.
--7
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0681-a" target="_blank">Page0681-a+ 56</a>]
Contraction of the prepuce.
--8 (In Rhet.)
A figure of speech in which there
is an exchange of a thing for what
is equal, less or greater;
परिवृत्तिर्विनिमयो योऽर्थानां स्यत्समासमैः
K. P. 10; e. g. दत्त्वा कटाक्षमेणाक्षी जग्राह
हृदयं मम । मया तु हृदयं दत्त्वा गृहीतो
मदनज्वरः ॥ S. D. 734.
--9
Substitution of one word for another
without affecting the sense; as in
शब्दपरिवृत्तिसहत्वं K. P. 10; e. g. in
वृषध्वज, ध्वज may be substituted by
लांछन or वाहन.
