परिसंख्या|परिसङ्ख्या
परिसंख्या
1 Enumeration,
computation.
--2 Sum, total, number;
वित्तस्य विद्यापरिसंख्यया मे R. 5. 21.
--3 (In Mīm. phil.) Exclusion,
specification, limitation to that which
is enumerated or expressly
mentioned, so that everything else is
excluded; (परिसंख्या is opposed to
विधि which lays down a rule for the
first time, and to नियम which restricts
the choice to an alternative which
is expressly stated when several
such alternatives are possible);
विधिरत्यंतमप्राप्तौ नियमः पाक्षिके सति ।
तत्र चान्यत्र च प्राप्तौ परिसंख्येति
गीयते ॥ e. g. पंच पंचनखा भक्ष्याः
usually quoted by the Mīmāṃsakas;
अयं नियमविधिर्न तु परिसंख्या Kull.
on Ms. 3. 45.
--4 (In Rhet.)
Special mention or exclusive
specification, i. e. where with or
without a query something is affirmed
for the denial, expressed or
understood, of something else
similar to it; (this figure is
particularly striking when it is based on
a श्लेष or pun); यस्मिन् महीं शासति
चित्रकर्मसु वर्णसंकराश्चापेषु गुणच्छेदाः &c. or
यस्य नूपुरेषु मुखरता विवाहेषु करग्रहणं तुरंगेषु
कशाभिघातः &c. K; for other examples
see S. D. 735.
--5 Recapitueation.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

