पिंग|पिङ्ग|पिङ्गं|पिङ्गः
पिंग a. [पिंज्-वर्णे अंच् न्यंक्व˚ कुत्वम्]
Reddish-brown, tawny, yellow-red.
अंतर्निविष्टामलपिंगतारं (विलोचनं)
Ku. 7. 33.
--गः
1 The tawny colour.
--2 A buffalo.
--3 A rat.
--गा
1
Turmeric.
--2 Saffron.
--3 A kind of
yellow pigment.
--4 An epithet of
Durgā.
--5 A bow-string.
--गं A
young animal.
--Comp.
--अक्ष a.
having reddish-brown eyes,
redeyed.
--(क्षः) {1} an ape. {2}
an epithet of Śiva.
--ईक्षणः
an epithet of Śiva.
--ईशः an
epithet of fire.
--कपिशा a species
of cock-roach.
--चक्षुस् m. a crab.
--जटः an epithet of Śiva.
--सारः
yellow orpiment.
--स्फटिकः ‘yellow
crystal’, a kind of gem (गोमेद).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिंगल|पिङ्गल|पिङ्गलं|पिङ्गलः
पिंगल a. [पिंग-सिध्मा˚ लच्, पिंगं
लाति, ला-क वा Tv.] Reddish-brown,
yellowish, brown, tawny;
R. 12. 71; Ms. 3. 8.
--लः
1 The tawny
colour.
--2 Fire.
--3 A monkey.
--4
An ichneumon.
--5 A small owl.
--6
A kind of snake.
--7 N. of an
attendant on the sun.
--8 N. of one
of Kubera's treasures.
--9 N. of a
reputed sage, the father of
Sanskrit prosody, his work being known
as पिगलच्छंदःशास्त्र; छंदोज्ञानानंधिं जघान
मकरो वेलातटे पिंगलं Pt. 2. 33.
--लं
1
Brass.
--2 Yellow orpiment.
--ला
1
A kind of owl.
--2 The Śiśu tree
(शिंशपा).
--3 A kind of metal.
--4
A particular vessel of the body.
--5
The female elephant of the south
--6 N. of a courtezan who became
remarkable for her piety and
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-b" target="_blank">Page0700-b+ 56</a>]
virtuous life; (the Bhāgavata
mentions how she and Ajamīḍha were
delivered from the trammels of the
world).
--Comp.
--अक्षः an
epithet of Śiva.
--लौहं brass.
