पुत्रका
पुत्रका, --पुत्रिका
1 A daughter.
--2
A doll, puppet.
--3 A daughter
appointed to raise male issue for a
father who has no sons; अपुत्रऽनेन
विधिना सुतां कुर्वीत पुत्रिकां । यदपत्यं
भवेदस्यां तन्मम स्यात्स्वधाकरम् ॥.
--4 The
cotton or down of the tamarisk.
--5
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0708-b" target="_blank">Page0708-b+ 57</a>]
(At the end of comp.) Anything
little or small of its kind; as in
असिपुत्रिका, खङ्गपुत्रिका &c.
--Comp.
--पुत्रः, --सुतः {1} a daughter's
son who by agreement becomes
the son of her father; see
Ms. 9. 127. {2} a daughter who, being
regarded as a son, returns to her
father's house; (पुत्रिकैव पुत्रः; अथवा
पुत्रिकैव सुतः पुत्रिकासुतः सोऽप्यौरससम एव
Mit. on Y. 2. 128). {3} a
grandson
--प्रसूः a mother of daughters.
--भर्तृ m. ‘a daughter's husband,’ a
son-in-law.
