प्रकाम|प्रकामं|प्रकामः
प्रकाम a.
1 Amorous.
--2
Excessive, much, to the heart's content,
at pleasure; प्रकामविस्तार R. 2. 11;
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-a" target="_blank">Page0724-a+ 55</a>]
प्रकामालोकनीयतां Ku. 2. 24.
--मः
Desire, pleasure, satisfaction.
--मं
ind.
1 Very much, exceedingly;
जातो ममायं विशदः प्रकामं (अंतरोत्मा)
Ś. 4. 21; R. 6. 44; Mk. 5. 25.
--2
Sufficiently, to the heart's content,
according to the wish or desire.
--3
Voluntarily, willingly;
Mu. 1. 25.
--भुज् a. eating till satisfied or
to the heart's content; R. 1. 66.
