R. 1. 44; 2. 22.
--3 To receive or accept
as a present.
--4 To receive
inimically, oppose, encounter, resist; to
attack, assault; प्रतिजग्राह
कालिंगस्तमस्त्रैर्गजसाधनः R. 4. 40; 12. 47.
--5
To take in marriage, marry;
Ms. 9. 72.
--6 To obey, conform or listen
to.
--7 To resort to, betake oneself
to.
--8 To eclipse.
--9 To assent to,
admit.
--10 To occupy, take
possession of.
--11 To deprive (one) of.
--12 To welcome, receive.
--13 To eat,
drink. --Caus.
1 To cause to accept,
give, present.
--2 To allow to take
or retain; मुष्टं प्रतिग्राहयता स्वमर्थं
पात्रीकृतो दस्युरिवासि येन Ś. 5. 20.
