प्रपद्
प्रपद् {c4c} A.
1 To enter upon, set
forward, set foot in.
--2 (a) To go
to or towards, approach, resort or
attain to, reach; तां जन्मने शैलवधूं प्रपेदे
Ku. 1. 21; (क्षितीशं) कौत्सः प्रपेदे
वरतंतुशिष्यः R. 5. 1; Bk. 4. 1;
Ki. 1. 9; 11. 16; R. 8. 11. (b) To take
shelter or refuge with, flee to for
safety, submit; शरणार्थमन्यां कथं
प्रपत्स्ये त्वयि दीप्यमाने R. 14. 64.
--3 To
go or come to a particular state,
arrive at, attain to, arrive at or be
in a particular condition; रेणुः प्रपेदे
पथि पंकभावं R. 16. 30;
मुहूर्तकर्णोत्पलतां प्रपेदे Ku. 7. 81; बाल्यात्परं साथ
वयः प्रपेदे Ku. 1. 31; 5. 24;
ईदृशीमवस्थां प्रपन्नोस्मि Ś. 5: ऋषिनिकरौरिति
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">Page0751-b+ 55</a>]
संशयः प्रपेदे Bv. 4. 33; Amaru. 27.
--4 To get, find, secure, obtain,
attain to; partake of share in;
सहकार न प्रपेदे मधुपेन भवत्समं जगति
Bv. 1. 21; कांतं वपुर्व्योमचरं प्रपेदे R. 5. 51.
--5 To behave or act towards, deal
with; किं प्रपद्यते वैदर्भः M. 1 ‘what
does he propose to do’; पश्यामो मयि
किं प्रपद्यते Amaru. 20.
--6 To admit,
allow, agree or consent to;
Y. 2. 40.
--7 To draw near, come on,
approach (as time &c.).
--8 To be
going on, to proceed.
--9 To take effect,
thrive, prosper.
--10 To throw
oneself down, fall down (at another's
feet).
--11 Ved. To attack, assault.
