प्रमद्
प्रमद् {c4c} P.
1 To be intoxicated or
drunk.
--2 To be careless about, to
be negligent or heedless, be
regardless of or indifferent to (with loc.);
अतोऽर्थान्न प्रमाद्यंति प्रमदासु विपश्चितः
Ms. 2. 213.
--3 To omit to do,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">Page0754-c+ 58</a>]
swerve or deviate from (with abl.)
स्वाधिकारात्प्रमत्तः Me. 1.
--4 To make
a mistake, err, go astray; Bk. 5. 8,
17. 39; 18. 8.
--5 To spend or while
a way (time).
