प्रशम्
प्रशम् {c4c} P.
1 To become calm or
tranquil.
--2 To be soothed or
appeased.
--3 To stop, cease, terminate.
--4 To be allayed, be quenched or
extinguished; प्रशांतं पावकास्त्रं U. 6;
Pt. 3. 56.
--5 To decay, wither
away. --Caus.
1 To soothe, appease,
pacify; Ms. 8. 391.
--2 To allay,
extinguish, quench, put down;
त्वामासारप्रशमितवनोपप्लवं Me. 17.
--3
To remove, put an end to; तं (
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-c" target="_blank">Page0762-c+ 57</a>]
अपचारं) अन्विष्य प्रशमयेः R. 15. 47.
--4 To conquer, vanquish, subdue;
Mk. 10. 60.
--5 To settle, adjust,
compose; प्रशमयसि विवादं कल्पसे
रक्षणाय Ś. 5. 8.
--6 To kill, destroy.
--7
To cure, heal.
