प्रसन्न|प्रसन्नः
प्रसन्न p. p.
1 Pure, clear, bright,
limpid, pellucid, transparent;
Ku. 1. 23; 7. 74; Ś. 5. 21.
--2 Pleased,
delighted, propitiated, soothed;
गंगां शरन्नयति सिंधुपतिं प्रसन्नां Mu. 3. 9;
गंभीरायाः पयसि सरितश्चेतसीव प्रसन्ने
Me. 40 (where the first sense is
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-b" target="_blank">Page0764-b+ 57</a>]
also intended); Ku. 5. 35;
R. 2. 68.
--3 Kind, kindly disposed,
gracious, propitious; अवेहि मां कामदुघां
प्रसन्नां R. 2. 63.
--4 Plain, open, clear,
easily intelligible (as meaning).
--5
True, correct; प्रसन्नस्ते तर्कः V. 2;
प्रसन्नप्रायस्ते तर्कः Māl. 1.
--6 Settled
down, tranquil.
--न्ना
1 Propitiation,
pleasing.
--2 Spirituous liquor.
--Comp.
--आत्मन् a.
gracious-minded, propitious. (--m.) N. of
Viṣṇu.
--ईरा spirituous liquor.
--कल्प a. {1} almost calm. {2} almost
true.
--मुख, --वदन a.
gracious-looking, with a pleased countenance,
smiling.
--सलिल a. having clear
water.
