बंधकः|बन्धक|बंधक|बन्धकं|बन्धकः
बंधकः
1 One who binds or
catches, a binder.
--2 A catcher.
--3 A band,
tie, rope, tether.
--4 A dike, bank,
dam.
--5 A pledge, deposit.
--6 A
posture of the body.
--7 Barter,
exchange.
--8 A violator, ravisher.
--9
A promise.
--10 A city.
--11 A part
or portion (at the end of num.
compounds); ऋणं सदशबंधकं Y. 2. 76.
--कं Binding, confinement.
--की
1
An unchaste woman; न मे त्वया
कौमारबंधक्या प्रयोजनं Māl. 7; Ve. 2.
--2
A harlot, courtezan; बलात् धृतोसि
मयेति बंधकीधाष्टर्यं K. 237.
--3 A female
elephant.
--4 A barren woman.
