भर्तृ|भर्त्तृ
भर्तृ m. [भृ-तृच्]
1 A husband;
यद्भर्तुरेव हितमिच्छति तत्कलत्रं
Bh. 2. 8; स्त्रीणां भर्ता धर्मदाराश्च पुंसां
Māl. 6. 18.
--2 A lord, master,
superior; भर्तुःशापेन Me. 1; गण˚, भूत˚ &c.
--3 A leader, commander, chief;
R. 7. 41.
--4 A supporter, bearer,
protector.
--5 The creator.
--6 N. of
Viṣṇu.
--Comp.
--घ्नी a woman
who murders her husband.
--दारकः a crown-prince, prince royal,
young prince, an heir-apparent (a
term of address chiefly used in
dramas).
--दारिका a young princess
(a term of address in dramas).
--व्रतं
fidelity or devotion to a husband.
--(ता) a virtuous and devoted wife;
cf. पतिव्रता.
--शोकः grief for the
death of the husband.
--हरिः N.
of a celebrated author to whom
are ascribed the three Śatakas (
शृंगार, नीति and वैराग्य) and also
वाक्यपदीय and भट्टिकाव्य.
