भ्रंश्
भ्रंश् {c1c} A., {c4c} P. (भ्रंशते, भ्रश्यति, भ्रष्ट;
with abl. in most cases)
1 To fall
or drop down, tumble; हस्ताद्भ्रष्टमिदं
बिसाभरणं Ś. 3. 26; Pt. 1. 130;
Śi. 18. 21.
--2 To fall from, deviate or
swerve from, stray from; यूथाद्भ्रष्टः
H. 4: R. 14. 16.
--3 To be deprived
of, lose; बभ्रंशेऽसौ धृतेस्त तः
Bk. 14. 71; Pt. 2. 108; 4. 37.
--4 To
escape, flee from; संग्रामात् बभ्रशुः
केचित् Bk. 14. 105; 15. 59.
--5 To
decline, decay, decrease.
--6 To
disappear, vanish, depart; Māl. 8. 12.
--Caus. (भ्रंशयति-ते)
1 To cause to
fall, throw or cast down.
--2 To
deprive of.
--3 To ruin, overturn.
--4 To cause to disappear or vanish.
--5 To expel.
