मनुष्य|मनुष्यः
मनुष्य a. [मनोरपत्यं यत् सुक् च],
Friendly or useful to man.
--ष्यः
1 A man, human being, mortal.
--2
A male.
--3 Ved. A class of manes.
--Comp.
--इंद्रः, ईश्वः a king,
sovereign; R. 2. 2.
--करः human
exertion or effort; cf. पुरुषकार.
--जातिः.
f. mankind, human race.
--देवः {1} a
king; R. 2. 52. {2} a god among^1
men, a Brāhmaṇa.
--धर्मः {1} the
duty of man. {2} the character of
man, human character.
--वर्मन m. an
epithet of Kubera.
--मारणं homicide.
--यज्ञः hospitality, hospitable
reception of guests, one of the five daily
acts of a house-holder; see नृयज्ञ.
--लोकः the world of mortals, the
earth.
--विश्, --विशा f.,
--विशं
human race, mankind.
--शोणितं
human blood; (पपौ) कुतूहलेनेव
मनुष्यशोणितं R. 3. 54.
--सभा {1} an
assembly of men. {2} a crowd, multitude.
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0842-c" target="_blank">Page0842-c+ 55</a>]
{3} a place of meeting, assembly.
[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.
