मंदर|मन्दर|मन्दरः
मंदर a.
1 Slow, tardy, dull.
--2
Thick, dense; firm.
--3 Large, bulky.
--रः
1 N. of a mountain (used by
the gods and demons as a
churningstick when they churned the ocean
for nectar); पृषतैर्मदरोद्धूतैः क्षारोमेय
हवाच्युतं R. 4. 27; अभिनवजलसुदर
धृतमदर ए Gīt. 1. शोभैव
मंदरक्षब्धक्षुभेतांभोधिवर्णना Śi. 2. 107; Ki. 5. 30.
--2 A necklace of pearls (of 8 or 16
strings).
--3 Heaven.
--4 A mirror.
--5 One of the five trees in Indra's
paradise; see मंदार.
--रं ind. Slowly,
sluggishly.
--Comp.
--आवासा,
--वासिनी of Durgā.
