मांधातृ|मान्धातृ
मांधातृ m. N. of a king of the
solar race, son of Yuvanāśva
(being born from his own belly). As
soon as he came out of the belly,
the sages said ‘कं एष धास्यति’;
whereupon Indra came down and said
‘मां धास्यति’; the boy was, therefore,
called Māndhātṛ.
