मित|मितः
मित p. p. [मि मा-वा-क्त]
1
Measured, meted or measured out.
--2
Measured off, bounded, defined.
--3
Limited, measured, moderate, little,
scanty, sparing, brief (words &c.);
पृष्टः सत्यं मितं ब्रूते स भृत्योर्हो महीभुजां
Pt. 1. 87; R. 9. 34.
--4 Measuring,
of the measure of; (at the end of
comp.), as in ग्रहवसुकरिचंद्रमिते वर्षे
i. e. in 1889.
--5 Investigated,
examined.
--6 Cast, thrown away.
--7
Built.
--8 Established, founded.
--Comp.
--अक्षर a. brief,
measured, short, concise; Ku. 5. 63. {2}
composed in verse, metrical.
--(रा)
N. of a celebrated commentary by
Vijñāneśvara on Yājñavalkya's
Smṛti.
--अर्थ a. of measured meaning.
--अर्थकः a cautious envoy.
--आहार
a. sparing in diet.
--(रः)
moderation in eating.
--द्रुः the sea.
--भाषिन्, --वाच् a. speaking little or
measured words; महीयांसः प्रकृत्या
मितभाषिणः Śi. 2. 13.
--भुक्त a.
moderate in diet.
--व्ययिन् a. frugal,
economical.
