मीलित|मीलितं
मीलित p. p. [मील्-क्त]
1 Shut,
closed.
--2 Twinkled.
--3
Half-opened, unblown.
--4 Vanished,
disappeared.
--5 Assembled, gathered
(for मिलित).
--तं (In Rhet.) A
figure of speech in which the
difference or distinction between two
objects is shown to be completely
obscured on account of their
similarity, whether natural or artificial, in
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0867-c" target="_blank">Page0867-c+ 55</a>]
some respects; it is thus defined by
Mammaṭa: --समेन लक्ष्मणा वस्तु वस्तुना
यन्निगृह्यते । निजेनागंतुना वापि तन्मीलितमिति
स्मृतं ॥ K. P. 10.
