मुंड|मुण्ड|मुण्डं|मुण्डः
मुंड a. [मुंड्-घञ्]
1 Shaved, bald.
--2 Lopped, stripped of top-leaves.
--3 Blunt, pointless.
--4 Ved.
Hornless.
--5 Low, mean.
--डः
1 A man
with a shaved or bald head.
--2 A
bald or shaven head.
--3 The
forehead.
--4 A barber.
--5 The trunk
of a tree stripped of its
top-branches.
--6 An epithet of Rāhu. --m.
pl. N. of a people.
--डा
1 N. of
a plant (मुंडीरिका).
--2 Bengal
madder.
--3 A female mendicant of a
particular order.
--डं
1 The head.
--2
Myrrh.
--3 Iron.
--Comp.
--अयसं iron.
--चणकः a kind of pulse (कलाय).
--फलः a cocoa-nut tree.
--मंडली {1} a
number of shaven heads. {2} a
number of troops of an inferior kind,
a mere crowd or mob; वरमल्पवलं सारं
न कुर्यान्मुंडमंडलीं H. 3. 89.
--लोहं iron.
--शालिः a kind of rice.
