रशना
रशना, रसना [अश्-युच् रशादेशः cf.
Uṇ. 2. 75]
1 A rope, cord.
--2 A
rein, bridle.
--3 A zone, girdle,
woman's girdle; रसतु रसनापि तव
घनजघनमंडले घोषयतु मन्मथनिदेशं Gīt. 10;
R. 7. 10, 8. 58; Me. 35.
--4 The
tongue; Bv. 1. 111.
--Comp.
--उपमा a variety of the figure उपमा; it is
‘a string or series’ of comparisons’
which consists in making the
Upameya in the first comparison the
Upamāna in the second, and so forth;
see S. D. 664.
--गुणः the cord of a
girdle.
