राका
राका [रा-क तस्य नेत्वम् Uṇ. 3. 40]
1 The full-moon day, particularly
the night; दारिद्र्यं भजते कलानिधिरयं
राकाधुना म्लायति Bv. 2. 72, 54, 94, 150,
165, 175; 3. 11.
--2 The goddess
presiding over the full-moon day.
--3 A girl in whom menstruation has
just commenced.
--4 Itch, scab.
--5
N. of the mother of खर and शुर्पणखा,
--Comp.
--ईशः {1} full moon. {2}
N. of Śiva.
--चंद्रः, --पतिः, --रमणः full
moon.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0907-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
