राक्षस|राक्षसः
राक्षस a. (सी f.) [रक्षस इदं अण्]
Belonging to or like an evil spirit,
demoniacal, partaking of a
demon's nature; मुनयो
राक्षसीमाहुर्वाचमुन्मत्तदृप्तयोः U. 5. 30, Bg. 9. 12.
--सः
1 A demon, an evil
spirit, a goblin, fiend, imp.
--2 One of
the eight forms of marriage in
Hindu Law, in which a girl is
forcibly seized and carried away after
the defeat or destruction of her
relatives in battle; राक्षसो युद्धहरणात्
Y. 1. 61; cf. Ms. 3. 33 also.
(Kṛṣṇa carried away Rukmiṇī in
this manner).
--3 One of the
astronomical Yogas.
--4 N. of a minister
of Nanda, an important character in
the Mudrārākṣasa.
--5 A king of
the Rākṣasas.
--सी
1 A female
demon.
--2 Laṅkā or Ceylon.
--3
Night.
--4 A larger tooth, tusk.
--Comp.
--इंद्रः N. of Rāvaṇa.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0907-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षा
राक्षा See लाक्षा; (perhaps an
incorrect form).
