लंब्|लम्ब्
लंब् {c1c} A. (लंबते, लंबित)
1 To hang
down, hang from, dangle; ऋषयो ह्यत्र
लंबते Mb.
--2 To be attached to,
stick to, hold on to, rest on;
ललंबिरे सदसिलताः प्रिया इव Śi. 7. 25;
प्रस्थानं ते कथमपि सखे लंबमानस्य भावि
Me. 41 (where लं˚ means ‘hanging,
down towards’ or ‘resting upon’
the back or hips).
--3 To go
down, sink, decline or hang down
(as the sun), fall down; लंबमाने
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0924-c" target="_blank">Page0924-c+ 57</a>]
दिवाकरे; Śi. 9. 20; Ki. 9. 1;
त्वदधरचुंबनलंबितकज्जलमुज्ज्वलय प्रिय लोचने
Gīt. 12 (= गलित).
--4 To fall or lag
behind.
--5 To delay, tarry.
--6 To
sound. --Caus. (लंबयति-ते)
1 To
let down, cause to hang down.
--2 To
hang up, suspend.
--3 To stretch
out, extend (as the hand); करेण
वातायनलंबितेन R. 13. 21; को
लंबयेदाहरणाय हस्तं 6. 75.
--4 To cause to
be attached, join.
--5 To depress.
--WITH उद् to stand up, stand
erect: पादेनैकेन गगने द्वितीयेन च भूतले ।
तिष्ठाम्युल्लंबितस्तावद्यावत्तिष्ठति भास्करः
Mk. 2. 10.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0924-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लंब|लम्ब|लम्बः
लंब a. [लंब्-अच्]
1 Hanging down,
hanging from, pendent, dangling;
पांड्योयमंसार्पितलंबहारः R. 6. 60, 84;
Me. 84.
--2 Hanging upon, attached
to.
--3 Great, large.
--4 Spacious.
--5
Long, tall.
--बः
1 A perpendicular.
--2 Co-latitude, the arc between the
pole of any place and the zenith,
complement of latitude.
--3 A bribe.
--Comp.
--उदर a. big-bellied,
pot-bellied, portly.
--(रः) {1} N. of
Gaṇeśa. {2} a glutton.
--ओष्ठः (
लंबो-बौ-ष्ठः) a camel.
--कर्णः {1} an
ass. {2} a goat. {3} an elephant. {4}
a falcon. {5} a demon or Rākṣasa.
--गुणः, --ज्या, --रेखा the sine of the
co-latitude.
--जठर a. pot-bellied,
portly.
--पयोधरा a woman with
large pendent breasts.
--स्फिच् a.
having fat or protuberant buttocks.
