लाक्षा
लाक्षा [लक्ष्यतेऽनया लक्ष् अच् पृषो˚
वृद्धिः]
1 A kind of red dye, lac;
(largely used by women in ancient
times as an article of decoration,
especially for the soles of the feet and
lips; cf. अलक्त; it is said to be
obtained from the cochineal insect and
from the resin of a particular tree);
निष्ठ्यूतश्चरणोपभोगसुलभो लाक्षारसः
केनाचित् (तरुणा) Ś. 4. 4; Rs. 6. 14;
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0927-a" target="_blank">Page0927-a+ 56</a>]
Ki. 5. 23.
--2 The insect which
produces the red dye.
--Comp.
--तरुः, --वृक्षः N. of a tree,
Butea Frondosa.
--प्रसादः, --प्रसाधनः the red
Lodhra tree.
--रक्त a. dyed with
lac.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0926-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

