लेपः|लेप
लेपः [लिप्-घञ्]
1 Smearing,
plastering, anointing; Y. 1. 188.
--2
An unguent, ointment, salve.
--3 A
plaster in general (such as
whitewash, mortar &c.).
--4 The wipings
of the hand (or the remnants of
the food sticking to the hand),
after offering funeral oblations to
the first three ancestors (पितृ, पितामह
and प्रपितामह), (these wipings being
offered to the three ancestors after
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0932-c" target="_blank">Page0932-c+ 56</a>]
the great-grand-father; i. e. to
paternal ancestors in the 4th, 5th
and 6th degrees); लेपभाज श्चतुर्थाद्याः
पित्राद्याः पिंडभागिनः.
--5 A spot,
stain, defilement, pollution.
--6
Moral impurity, sin.
--7 Food.
--Comp.
--करः a plaster maker,
white-washer, bricklayer.
--भागिन्, --भुज् m. a
paternal ancestor in the 4th, 5th
and 6th degree; Ms. 3. 216.
