वत्
वत् a.
1 An affix added to nouns
to show ‘possession’; धनवत्
possessed of wealth; रूपवत् beautiful;
so भगवत्, भास्वत् &c.; (the words
so formed being adjectives).
--2
Added to the base of the past passive
participle वत् turns it into a past
active participle; इत्युक्तवंतं
जनकात्मजायां R. 14. 43. --ind. An affix
added to nouns or adjectives to
denote ‘likeness’ or ‘resemblance’
and may be translated by ‘like’,
‘as’; आत्मवत्सर्वभूतानि यः पश्यति स
पंडितः.
