वलयः|वलय|वलयं
वलयः --यं [वल्-अयन्]
1 A
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0951-a" target="_blank">Page0951-a+ 55</a>]
bracelet, armlet;
विहितविशदबिसकिसलयवलया जीवति परमिह तव रतिकलया
Gīt. 6; Bk. 3. 22; Me. 2, 60;
R. 13. 21, 43.
--2 A ring, coil; Ś. 1. 33,
7. 11.
--3 The zone or girdle of a
married woman.
--4 A circle,
circumference (oft. at the end of comp.);
भ्रांतभूवलयः Dk.; वेलावप्रवलयां (उर्वी)
R. 1. 30; दिग्वलय Śi. 9. 8.
--5 An
enclosure, a bower; as in लतावलयमंडप.
--यः
1 A fence, hedge.
--2 A branch.
--3 A sore throat. (वलयीकृ ‘to form
into a bracelet;’ Ku. 5. 66; वलयीभू
‘to serve as a bracelet or girdle’).
