वह्निः|वह्नि
वह्निः [वह्-नि]
1 Fire; अतृणे
पतितो वह्निः स्वयमेवोपशाम्यति Subhāṣ.
--2 The digestive faculty, gastric
fluid.
--3 Digestion, appetite.
--4 A
vehicle.
--5 The marking-nut plant.
--6 Lead-wort.
--7 A sacrificer, priest.
--8 A god in general.
--9 An epithet
of the Maruts.
--10 Of Soma.
--11
A horse.
