विदूर|विदूरः
विदूर a. Remote, distant;
सरिद्विदूरांतरभावतन्वी R. 13. 48;
U. 6. 39.
--रः N. of a mountain or city
from which the Vaidūrya jewel or
lapis lazuli is brought;
विदूरभूमिर्नवमेघशब्दादुद्भिन्नया रत्नशलाकयेव
Ku. 1. 24; see Malli thereon, as well as
on Śi. 3. 45. (The forms विदूरं,
विदूरेण, विदूरतस् or विदूरात् are often
used adverbially in the sense of
‘from a distance,’ ‘from afar’, ‘at
a distance’, ‘far off’; Māl. 3. 18.).
--Comp.
--ग a. spreading far and
wide.
--जं the lapis lazuli.
