विनी
विनी {c1c} P.
1 To remove, take
away, destroy (said to be Atm.
only except where it has ‘a part of
the body’ for its object);
पटुपटहध्वनिभिर्विनीतनिद्रः R. 9. 71; विनीतखेदः
13. 35, 46; 15. 48; Śi. 10. 62,
Ki. 7. 30, Ku. 1. 9, 5. 32.
--2 To teach,
instruct, educate, train; विनिन्युरेनं
गुरवो गुरुप्रियं R. 3. 29; 5. 101.
15. 69; 18. 51; Y. 1. 311; Ku. 1. 34.
--3 To tame, subdue, govern,
control (fig. also); वन्यान्विनेष्यन्निव दुष्ट
सत्वान् R. 2. 8; 6. 27, 14. 75;
Ki. 2. 41; वनगज इव
तस्मात्सोभ्युपायैर्विनेयः Mu. 3. 25.
--4 To appease, pacify
(anger) (Atm.); R. 2. 49.
--5
To pass away, spend (as time);
कथमपि यामिनीं विनीय Gīt. 8.
--6 To
carry through, perform, complete,
finish.
--7 To spend, apply to use
(Atm.). शतं विनयते Sk.
--8 To give,
present, pay, pay off (as tribute)
(Atm.); करं विनयते Sk.
--9 To
lead or conduct towards;
Ku. 7. 9.
--10 To bid, direct, order;
Ku. 3. 41.
--11 To bend down, incline.
--12 To spread, stretch out.
