विनय|विनयः
विनय a.
1 Cast, thrown.
--2
Secret.
--3 Ill-behaved.
--यः
1
Guidance, discipline, instruction (in
one's duties), moral training;
प्रजानां विनयाधानात् R. 1. 24;
Māl. 10. 5.
--2 Sense of propriety,
decorum, decency; अनुयास्यन्मुनितनयां
सहसा विनयेन वारितप्रसरः Ś. 1. 29.
--3 Polite conduct, gentleman-like
bearing, good breeding or manners;
R. 6. 79; Māl. 1. 18.
--4 Modesty,
humility; सुष्ठु शोभसे आर्यपुत्र एतेन
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-a" target="_blank">Page0980-a+ 56</a>]
विनयमाहात्म्येन U. 1; विद्या ददाति वि
नयम्; तथापि नीचैर्विनयाददृश्यत
R. 3. 34; 10. 71 (where Malli. renders
विनय by इंद्रियजय or restraint of
passions, unnecessarily in our opinion^1).
--5 Reverence, courtesy, obeisance.
--6 Conduct in general.
--7 Drawing
off, taking away, removing;
Śi. 10. 42.
--8 A man who has subdued his
senses.
--9 A trader, merchant.
--Comp.
--अवनत a. stooping
humbly.
--ग्राहिन् a. tractable, obedient,
submissive.
--भाज् a. modest,
wellbehaved.
--वाच् a. speaking mildly
or affably.
--स्थ a. modest.
[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.
