विप्लु
विप्लु {c1c} A.
1 To float about, swing
to and fro, fluctuate.
--2 To drift (in
the sea), be scattered; यदि न
स्यान्नरपतिः सम्यङ् नेता ततः प्रजा । अकर्णधारा
जलधौ विप्लवेतेह नैरिव H. 3. 2,
Pt. 3. 73.
--3 To be confused (as mind).
--4 To be ruined or destroyed.
--5
To fail. --Caus.
1 To cause to float
or swim.
--2 To divulge, spread
abroad.
--3 To teach (to unworthy
persons); Ms. 11. 199.
--4 To cause
to fail, spoil, mar;
गुणानामायथातर्थ्यादर्थं विप्लावयंति ये Śi. 2. 56.
--5 To
confound, bewilder.
