विमर्दः|विमर्द|विमर्द्द|विमर्द्दः
विमर्दः
1 Pounding, crushing,
bruising.
--2 Rubbing together,
trituration (as of perfumes),
friction; विमर्दसुरभिर्बकुलावलिका खल्वहं
M. 3; R. 5. 65; कस्तूरिका
मृगविमर्दसुगंधिरेति Śi. 4. 61, 11. 28.
--3
Pressing together (as in embrace).
--4 Spoiling, marring;
कुतूहलविमर्दकारिणा परिश्रमेण Mk. 1.
--5 Touch;
contact.
--6 Rubbing the person
with saffron or other unguents.
--7
War, battle, fight, encounter;
विमर्दक्षमां भूमिमवतरावः U. 5, 3. 44.
--8
Destruction, devastation; R. 6. 62.
--9 Conjunction of the sun and
moon.
--10 An eclipse.
--11
Weariness, tediousness.
