विरंचिः|विरञ्चि|विरंचि|विरञ्चिः
विरंचः, --चिः N. of Brahman.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरंज्|विरञ्ज्
विरंज् {c1c} {c4c} U.
1 To grow
discoloured or soiled, be coarse or
rough; केशा अपि विरज्यंते निःस्नेहाः
किं न सेवकाः Pt. 1. 82 (where it
has sense 2 also).
--2 To be
discontented or disaffected, to dislike,
hate; चिरानुरक्तोऽपि विरज्यते जनः
Mk. 1. 53; यां चिंतयामि सततं मयि सा
विरक्ता Bh. 2. 2; Bk. 18. 22.
--3 To
become disgusted with the world
and hence to renounce all worldly
attachments. --Caus. To colour,
dye.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्त|विरक्तः
विरक्त p. p.
1 Very red, ruddy,
R. 13. 64.
--2 Discoloured.
--3
Changed in mind, disaffected, displeased;
Bh. 2. 2.
--4 Free from passion or
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">Page0988-a+ 56</a>]
worldly attachment, indifferent.
--5
Impassioned.
--क्ता An unfortunate
or unhappy woman.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्तिः|विरक्ति
विरक्तिः f.
1 Change of disposition,
dissatisfaction, discontent,
disaffection.
--2 Estrangement.
--3
Indifference, absence of desire, freedom
from passion or worldly
attachment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरटः|विरट
विरटः A kind of black
agallochum.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरणं|विरण
विरणं A kind of fragrant grass;
cf. वीरण.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरम्
विरम् {c1c} P.
1 To end, terminate,
come to an end; अविदितगतयामा
रात्रिरेव व्यरंसीत् U. 1. 27; 6. 33.
--2
To cease, desist, stop, leave off
(speaking &c.); एतावदुक्त्वा विरते
मृगेंद्रे R. 2. 51; Śi. 2. 13; oft. with
abl.; हा हंत किमिति चित्तं विरमति
नाद्यपि विषयेभ्यः Bv. 4. 25; न स्थिरकर्मा
विरराम कर्मणः R. 8. 22;
वत्सैतस्माद्विरम विरमातः परं न क्षमोस्मि U. 1. 33;
Bh. 2. 80.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरत|विरतः
विरत p. p.
1 Ceased or desisting
from (with abl.).
--2 Rested,
stopped, ceased.
--3 Ended, concluded,
at an end; विरतं गेयमृतुर्निरुत्सवः
R. 8. 66.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरतिः|विरति
विरतिः f.
1 Cessation, stop,
discontinuance.
--2 Rest, end, pause.
--3 Indifference to worldly
attachments; विरतिवनितासंगमुदितः Bh. 3. 79.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरमः|विरम
विरमः
1 Cessation, stop.
--2
Sunset.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरामः|विराम
विरामः
1 (a) Cessation,
discontinuance; सुधां विना न प्रययुर्विरामं
Bh. 2. 80; प्रवृत्तस्याविरामे भवंती शासितव्या
Mbh. (b) Rest, repose.
--2 End,
termination, conclusion;
रजनिरिदानीमियमपि याति विरामं Gīt. 5;
U. 3. 16, Māl. 9. 34.
--3 Pause, stop.
--4
The stop or pause of the voice;
Mk. 3. 5.
--5 A small oblique stroke
placed under a consonant, usually
at the end of a sentence.
--6 N. of
Viṣṇu.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरल|विरलं|विरलः
विरल a.
1 Having interstices,
separated by intervals, thin, not
thick or compact; विपर्यासं यातो
घनविरलभावः क्षितिरुहां U. 2. 27; 1. 20;
भवति विरलभक्तिर्म्लानपुष्पापहारः
R. 5. 74.
--2 Fine, delicate.
--3 Loose,
wide apart.
--4 Rare, scarcely found,
unfrequent; विरला हि तेषामुपदेष्टारः
K.; Pt. 1. 29.
--5 Few, little
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">Page0988-b+ 56</a>]
(referring to number or quantity);
तत्त्वं किमपि काव्यानां जानाति विरलो
भुवि Bv. 1. 117; विरलातपच्छविः
Śi. 9. 3.
--6 Remote, distant, long (as
time, distance &c.).
--लं Curds,
coagulated milk.
--लं ind. Scarcely,
rarely, not frequently.
--Comp.
--जानुक a. bandy-legged,
bowkneed.
--द्रवा a kind of gruel.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरस|विरसः
विरस a.
1 Tasteless, insipid,
flavourless.
--2 Unpleasant,
disagreeable, painful; तावत्कोकिल विरसान्
यापय दिवसान् वनांतरे निवसन्
Bv. 1. 7; Māl. 1. 31; 6. 10.
--3 Cruel,
unfeeling.
--सः Pain.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहः|विरह
विरहः
1 Parting with,
separation.
--2 Especially, the separation
of lovers; सा विरहे तव दीना Gīt. 4;
क्षणमपि विरहः पुरा न सेहे ibid.;
Me. 8, 12, 29, 85, 87.
--3 Absence.
--4
Want.
--5 Desertion, abandonment,
relinquishment.
--6 The feeling of
love in separation; see विप्रलंभ (6).
--7
Loneliness.
--Comp.
--अनलः the fire
of separation.
--अवस्था the state
of separation.
--आर्त, --उत्कंठ,
--उत्सुक a. suffering from separation,
pining away in separation.
--उत्कंठिता a woman distressed by the
absence of her lover or husband,
one of the several classes of a
Nāyikā in poetic compositions; see
S. D. 121.
--ज्वरः the fever or
anguish of separation.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहिणी
विरहिणी
1 A woman separated
from her lover or husband.
--2
Wages, hire.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहित|विरहितः
विरहित p. p.
1 Deserted,
abandoned, forsaken.
--2 Separated from.
--3 Lonely, solitary.
--4 Bereft
of, devoid or destitute of, free from
(mostly in comp.).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहिन्
विरहिन् a. (णी f.)
1 Absent
from, being separated from a
mistress or lover; नृत्यति युवतिजनेन समं
सखि विरहिजनस्य दुरंते Gīt. 1.
--2
Lonely, solitary.
