विराज्
विराज् m.
1 Beauty, splendour.
--2 A man of the Kṣatriya or
warrior tribe.
--3 The first progeny
of Brahman; cf. Ms. 1. 32;
तस्मात् विराडजायत Rv. 10. 90. 5
(where विराज् is represented as born
from Puruṣa).
--4 The body.
--5
(In Vedānta phil.) N. of
‘intellect’ considered as ruling over the
aggregate of bodies. --f. N. of a
Vedic metre.
