विलुप्
विलुप् {c6c} P.
1 To break off, pull
out, cut off.
--2 To seize, plunder,
rob, carry off.
--3 To mar, spoil,
impair.
--4 (a) To destroy, ruin,
cause to disappear;
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">Page0991-c+ 55</a>]
प्रियमत्यंतविलुप्तदर्शनं Ku. 4. 2 ‘for ever lost to view’.
