वीत|वीतं|वीतः
वीत p. p. [वि˚इ-क्त]
1 Gone,
disappeared.
--2 Gone away,
departed.
--3 Let go, loosed, set free.
--4
Excepted, exempt.
--5 Approved,
liked.
--6 Unfit for war.
--7 Tame,
quiet.
--8 Freed from, devoid of
(mostly in comp.); वीतचिंत,
वीतस्पृह, वीतभी, वीतशंक &c.
--9 Desired,
wished for.
--10 Put on or worn
--तः An elephant or horse unfit or
untrained for war.
--तं Pricking (an
elephant) with the goad and
striking with the legs; वीतवीतभया नागाः
Ku. 6. 39 v. l. (see Malli. thereon);
निर्धूतवीतमपि बालकमुल्ललंतं Śi. 5. 47.
--Comp.
--दंभ a. humble, lowly.
--भय a. fearless, intrepid.
--(यः)
an epithet of Viṣṇu.
--मल a. pure.
--राग a. {1} free from desire;
Ku. 6. 39 v. l. {2} free from passion.
calm, tranquil. {3} colourless.
--(गः)
{1} a sage who has subdued his
passions. {2} a deified Jaina saint.
--शोकः (= अशोकः) the Aśoka tree.
--सूत्रं
the sacred thread.
