वेदिः|वेदि
वेदिः [विद्-इन्] A learned man,
sage, Paṇḍita.
--दिः, -दी f.
1 An
altar especially one prepared for a
sacrifice; अमी वेदिं परितः कॢप्तधिष्ण्याः
(वह्रयः) Ś. 4. 7.
--2 An altar of a
particular shape, the middle points
of which come very close to each
other; मध्येन सा वेदिविलग्नमध्या
Ku. 1. 39; (some propose to take वेदि in
this passage as meaning ‘a
sealring’).
--3 A quadrangular spot
in the court-yard of a temple or
palace.
--4 A seal-ring.
--5 N. of
Sarasvatī.
--6 A tract or region.
--Comp.
--ईशः {1} N. of Agni. {2} of
Brahman.
--जा an epithet of
Draupadi who was born from the midst
of the sacrificial altar of king
Drupada.
