शकुनिः|शकुनि
शकुनिः [शक्-उनि]
1 A bird;
तरुशकुनिकुरंगान् मैथिली यानपुष्यत्
U. 3. 25; Ms. 12. 63.
--2 A vulture,
kite or eagle.
--3 A cock.
--4 N. of
a son of Subala, king of Gāndhāra
and brother of Gāndhārī, wife of
Dhṛtarāṣṭra; he was thus the
maternal uncle of Duryodhana whom
he assisted in many of his wicked
schemes to exterminate the
Pāṇḍavas. The name is now
usually applied to an old wicked-minded
relative whose counsels tend to
ruin.
--5 N. of a demon killed by
Kṛṣṇa.
--Comp.
--ईश्वरः N. of
Garuḍa.
--प्रपा a trough for
watering birds.
--वादः {1} the cry or
sound of a bird. {2} the crowing of
a cock.
