tree), stump, pollard.
--6 The pin
of a dial.
--7 A measure of twelve
fingers.
--8 A measuring-rod
--9 The
sine of altitude (in astr.).
--10 Ten
billions.
--11 The fibres of a leaf.
--12 An ant-hill.
--13 The penis.
--14
The skate-fish.
--15 A demon.
--16 Poison.
--17 Sin; crime.
--18
An aquatic animal, particularly,
a goose.
--19 N. of Śiva.
--20
The sāla tree.
--21 A kind of
perfume (नखी).
--22 N. of Kāma, the
god of love.
