शम्
शम् ind. A particle meaning
welfare, happiness, prosperity,
health, and generally used to
express a blessing or pious wish,
(with dat. or gen.); शं देवदत्ताय
or देवदत्तस्य (often used in modern
letters as an auspicious conclusion;
इति शम्).
--Comp.
--कर see s. v.
--ताति a. conferring happiness,
propitious, auspicious.
--पाकः {1}
lac, red dye. {2} cooking,
maturing.
--भु see s. v.
