शाखा
शाखा
1 A branch (as of a tree);
आवज्र्य शाखाः R. 16. 19.
--2 An
arm.
--3 A party, section, faction.
--4 A part of subdivision of a work.
--5 A school, branch, sect.
--6 A
part or division of an animal.
--7 A
school or traditional recension of
the Veda, the traditional text
followed by a school; as in
शाकलशाखा, आश्वलायनशाखा, बाष्कलशाखा &c.
--Comp.
--चंक्रमणं leaping from
branch to branch’, irregular study.
--चंद्रन्यायः see under न्याय.
--नगरं, --पुरं
a suburb.
--पित्तः inflammation of the
extremities of the body, e. g. hands,
shoulders &c.
--भृत् m. a tree.
--भेदः difference of (Vedic) school.
--मृगः {1} a monkey, an ape. {2} a
squirrel.
--रंडः ‘a traitor to his
Śākhā’, a Brāhmaṇa who has
changed his own school of the Vedas.
--रथ्या a branch-road.
--विलीन a.
sitting on branches (as a bird).
--शिफा a root growing from a
branch (as of the fig-tree).
