शूद्रः|शूद्र
शूद्रः [शुच्-रक् पृषो˚ चस्य दः दीर्घः
Uṇ. 2. 19] A man of the fourth
or the last of the four principal
tribes of the Hindus; he is said
to have been born from the feet of
Puruṣa; पद्भ्यां शूद्रो अजायत
Rv. 10. 90. 12, or of Brahman;
Ms. 1. 87, and his principal business
was to serve the three higher castes;
cf. Ms. 1. 91.
--Comp.
--आर्ता
the Priyaṅgu plant.
--अह्निकं the
daily ceremonies or observances of
a Śūdra.
--उदकं water polluted by
the touch of a Śūdra.
--कृत्यं, --धर्मः
the duties of a Śūdra.
--प्रियः an
onion.
--प्रेष्यः a man of any of
the three higher castes who has
become a servant to a Śūdra.
--भूयिष्ठ a. consisting mostly of
Śūdras.
--याजकः one who conducts
a sacrifice for a Śūdra.
--वर्गः the
Śūdra or servile class.
--सेवनं
serving a Śūdra, being the servant of
a Śūdra.
