संसारः|संसार
संसारः
1 Course, passage.
--2 The
course or circuit of worldly life,
secular life, mundane^1 existence, the
world; असारः संसारः U. 1;
Māl. 5. 30; संसारधन्वभुवि किं सारमामृशसि
शंसाधुना शुभमते Aśvad. 22; or
परिवर्तिनि संसारे मृतः को वा न जायते
Pt. 1. 27.
--3 Transmigration,
metempsychosis, succession of births.
--4
Worldly illusion.
--Comp.
--गमनं
transmigration.
--गुरुः {1} an
epithet of the god of love. {2}
the preceptor of the world.
--चक्रं succession of births and
deaths, metempsychosis.
--मार्गः {1}
the course of worldly affairs,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">Page1072-b+ 56</a>]
worldly life. {2} the vulva.
--मोक्षः,
--मोक्षणं final liberation or
emancipation from worldly life.
[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.
