कलिंदकन्यामंदाकिन्यौ संगच्छेते A. R. 7.
--2 To
cohabit, have sexual intercourse
with; भार्या च परसंगता Pt. 1. 238;
Ms. 8. 378.
--3 To keep company
or intercourse with, associate with.
--4 To agree, harmonize, be
suitable.
--5 To become contracted,
shrink up.
--6 To die, depart.
--7
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-a" target="_blank">Page1079-a+ 56</a>]
To go to, attain (with acc.). --Caus.
1 To bring together, join, unite;
वधूवरौ संगमयांचकार R. 7. 20.
--2 To
endow or present with, unite with,
bestow on, give to; प्रियसुहृदि
बिभीषणे संगमय्य श्रियं वैरिणः R. 12. 104.
