समाधा
समाधा {c3c} U.
1 To place or put
together, join, unite.
--2 To place,
put, put or place upon, apply to;
पदं मूर्ध्नि समाधत्ते केसरी मत्तदंतिनः
Pt. 1. 327.
--3 To install, place on the
throne; R. 17. 8.
--4 To compose,
collect (as the mind); मनः
समाधाय निवृत्तशोकः Rām.; न शशाक
समाधातुं मनो मदनवेपितं Bhāg.
--5 To
concentrate, fix or apply intently
upon (as the eye, mind &c.);
Bg. 12. 9; Bh. 3. 48.
--6 To satisfy,
clear or solve (a doubt), answer
an objection; इति समाधत्ते (in
commentaries).
--7 To repair, redress,
set right, remove; न ते शक्याः
समाधातुं H. 3. 37; उत्पन्नामापदं यस्तु
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-b" target="_blank">Page1096-b+ 57</a>]
समाधत्ते स बुद्धिमान् 4. 7.
--8 To think
over; Bk. 12. 6.
--9 To entrust,
commit to, deliver over.
--10 To
produce, effect, accomplish.
--11
To place a burden, load.
--12 To
assume, take upon oneself.
--13 To
conceive (in the womb).
--14 To
establish.
