संभू|सम्भू
संभू {c1c} A.
1 To arise, to be born
or produced, spring up; कथमपि
भुवनेऽस्मिंस्तादृशाः संभवंति Māl. 2. 9;
धर्मसंस्थापनार्थाय संभवामि युगे युगे
Bg. 4. 8; Ki. 5. 22; Bk. 6. 138;
Ms. 8. 155.
--2 To be, become, exist.
--3
To happen, occur, take place.
--4
To be possible.
--5 To be adequate
for, be competent for (with inf.);
न यन्नियंतुं समभावि भानुना Śi. 1. 27.
--6 To meet, be united or joined
with; संभूयांभोधिमभ्येति महानद्या
नगापगा Śi. 2. 100; संभूयेव सुखानि चेतसि
Māl. 5. 9, 18.
--7 To be consistent.
--8
To have sexual intercourse with.
--9
To be capable of existing in, be
contained in. --Caus.
1 To
produce, effect, make.
--2 To imagine,
conceive, fancy, think.
--3 To guess or
conjecture; Ś. 2.
--4 To consider,
regard.
--5 To honour, respect,
esteem, show respect to; प्राप्तोऽसि
संभावयितुं वनान्मां R. 5. 11; 7. 8.
--6 To
honour or present with, treat with;
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-c" target="_blank">Page1105-c+ 57</a>]
Ku. 3. 37.
--7 To ascribe or impute
to; Mk. 1. 36.
--8 To come or
go to, approach.
--9 To take
part in, enjoy; U. 4.
--10 To
greet, salute.
--11 To manifest,
exhibit.
--12 To expect. --Pass. of
caus. To be possible; कथमेतद्भवति
संभाव्यते Ś. 2.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभवः|सम्भव|संभव|सम्भवः
संभवः
1 Birth, production,
springing up, arising, existence; प्रियस्य
सुहृदो यव मम तत्रैव संभवो भूयात्
Māl. 9; मानुषीषु कथं वा स्यादस्य रूपस्य
संभवः Ś. 1. 26; Bg. 3. 14; oft. at
the end of comp. in this sense;
अप्सरः संभवैषा Ś. 1.
--2 Production and
bringing up; Ms. 2. 227; (see
Kull. thereon).
--3 Cause, origin,
motive.
--4 Mixing, union,
combination.
--5 Possibility; संयोगो हि
वियोगस्य संसूचयति संभवं Subhāṣ.
--6 Compatibility, consistency.
--7
Adaptation, appropriateness.
--8
Agreement, conformity.
--9 Capacity.
--10 Equivalence (one of the
Pramāṇas).
