सर्वतस्|सर्व्वतस्
सर्वतस् ind.
1 From every side
or quarter.
--2 On all sides,
everywhere, all round.
--3 Completely,
entirely.
--Comp.
--गामिन् a. {1}
having access everywhere;
Ku. 3. 12. {2} all-pervading.
--भद्रः
{1} the car of Viṣṇu. {2} a
bamboo. {3} a kind of verse
artificially arranged; e. g. see
Ki. 15. 25. {4} a temple or palace having
openings on four sides; (n. also
in this sense). {5} the Nimba
tree. {6} a kind of military array.
--(द्रा) a dancing girl, an actress.
--मुख a. of every kind, complete,
unlimited; Ś. 5. 26.
--(खः) {1}
an epithet of Śiva. {2} of
Brahman; Ku. 2. 3 (having faces on
all sides). {3} the Supreme Being.
{4} the soul. {5} a Brāhmaṇa. {6}
fire. {7} heaven or Svarga (of
Indra).
--(खं) {1} water. {2} sky.
--शुभा the Priyaṅgu plant.
