साक्षात्
साक्षात् ind.
1 In the presence
of, before the very eyes, visibly,
openly, evidently.
--2 In person,
actually, in bodily form; साक्षात्
प्रियामुपगतामपहाय पूर्वं Ś. 6. 15;
1. 6.
--3 Directly. In comp. it is often
translated by ‘incarnate’;
साक्षाद्यमः; or by ‘open, direct’;
तत्साक्षात्प्रतिषेधः कोपाय Māl. 1. 11. (
साक्षात्कृ {1} to see with one's own eyes,
realize personally. {2} to have an
intuitive perception or manifestation
of; साक्षात्कृतधर्माण ॠषयः U. 7).
--Comp.
--करणं {1} causing to be
visibly present, {2} making evident
to the senses. {3} intuitive
perception.
--कारः perception,
apprehension, knowledge.
