साहसं|साहस|साहसः
साहसं [सहसा बलेन निर्वृत्तं अण्]
1
Violence, force, rapine; Ms. 7. 48.
--2 Any criminal act (such as
robbery, rape, felony &c.), a heinous
crime, an aggressive act.
--3 Cruelty,
oppression; Śi. 9. 59.
--4 Boldness,
daring, daring courage; साहसे श्रीः
प्रतिवसति Mk. 4.
--5 Precipitation,
rashness, temerity, an inconsiderate or
reckless act, a rash or daring act;
तदपि साहसाभासं Māl. 2; किमपरमतो
निर्व्यूढं यत्करार्पणसाहसं 9. 10;
Pt. 1. 191; Ki. 17. 42.
--6 Punishment,
chastisement, fine (m. also in this
sense), see Ms. 8. 138; Y. 1. 66,
365.
--Comp.
--अंकः {1} an epithet
of king Vikramāditya. {2} of a poet.
{3} of a lexicographer.
--अध्यवसायिन् a. acting rashly or with
inconsiderate haste.
--एकरसिक a.
wholly intent on violence, ferocious,
brutal.
--कारिन् a. {1} bold,
audacious. {2} rash, inconsiderate.
--लांछन
a. characterized by boldness.
