स्तंबः|स्तम्ब|स्तंब|स्तम्बः
स्तंबः [स्था-अबच् किच्च पृषो˚
Uṇ. 4. 96]
1 A clump of grass &c.;
R. 5. 15.
--2 A sheaf of corn; as
in स्तंबकरिता q. v.
--3 A cluster,
clump or bunch (in general);
U. 2. 29, R. 15. 19.
--4 A bush, thicket.
--5 A shrub or plant having no
decided stem.
--6 The post to which an
elephant is tied.
--7 A post.
--8
Stupefaction, insensibility;
(probably for स्तंभ in these two senses).
--9 A mountain.
--Comp.
--करि a.
forming sheaves or clusters.
--(रिः)
corn, rice.
--करिता forming sheaves
or clusters, abundant or luxuriant
growth; न शालेः स्तंबकरिता
बप्तुर्गुणमपेक्षते Mu. 1. 3.
--घनः {1} a small
hoe for weeding clumps of grass.
{2} a sickle for cutting corn. {3} a
basket for holding the heads of
wild rice.
--घ्नः, --घातः --हन्, --हननं --नी
a sickle for cutting corn, a
hoe.
--पुरं N. of a city (ताम्रलिप्त).
