स्ना
स्ना {c2c} P. (स्नाति, स्नात)
1 To
bathe, perform ablution;
मृगतृष्णांभसि स्नातः.
--2 To perform the
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-b" target="_blank">Page1151-b+ 58</a>]
ceremony of bathing at the time of
leaving the house of one's spiritual
preceptor. --Caus. (स्नापयति-ते,
स्नपयति-ते) To cause to bathe, wet,
moisten, sprinkle; (तोयैः) सतूर्यमेनां
स्नपयांबभूवुः Ku. 7. 10;
स्मितस्नपिताधरा Gīt. 12, U. 3. 23,
Ki. 5. 44. 47; Śi. 2. 7, Me. 43. --Desid. (
सिस्नासति) To wish to bathe. -WITH
अप to bathe after mourning.
--नि
to plunge deep into; i. e. to be
perfect or thoroughly versed in;
see निष्णात.
