स्वधा
स्वधा [स्वद्-आ पृषो˚ दस्य धः]
1
One's own nature or determination,
spontaneity.
--2 One's own will or
pleasure.
--3 The oblation of food
offered to the Pitṛs or Manes
of deceased ancestors;
स्वधासंग्रहतत्पराः R. 1. 66, Ms. 9. 142,
Y. 1. 102.
--4 The food offered to the
Manes personified.
--5 Food or
oblation in general.
--6 One's own
portion or share.
--7 A Śrāddha or
funeral ceremony.
--8 N. of Māyā
or illusion. --ind. An
exclamation uttered on offering an oblation
to the Manes (with dat.); पितृभ्यः
स्वधा Sk.
--Comp.
--कर a.
offering oblations to the Pitṛs.
--कारः
the exclamation Svadhā; पूतं हि
तद्गृहं यत्र स्वधाकारः प्रवर्तते.
--निनयनं a
formula or sacred text used in
making the oblations to the Pitṛs.
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">Page1160-a+ 56</a>]
--प्रियः {1} Agni or fire. {2} black
sesamum.
--भुज् m. {1} a deceased or
deified ancestor. {2} a god, deity.
