स्वामिन्
स्वामिन् a. (नी f.) [स्व-अस्त्यर्थे मिनि
दीर्घः] Possessing proprietory rights.
--m.
1 A proprietor, an owner.
--2
A lord, master; रघुस्वामिनः सच्चरित्रं
Vikr. 18. 107.
--3 A sovereign,
king, monarch.
--4 A husband.
--5
A spiritual preceptor.
--6 A
learned Brāhmaṇa, an ascetic or
religious man of the highest order;
(in this sense usually added to
proper names).
--7 An epithet of
Kārtikeya.
--8 Of Viṣṇu.
--9 Of Śiva.
--10 Of the sage Vātsyāyana.
--11
Of Garuḍa.
--Comp.
--उपकारकः a
horse.
--कार्यं the business of a
king or master.
--जंघिन् m. N. of
Paraśurāma.
--पाल m. du. the
owner and the keeper (of cattle);
Ms. 8. 5.
--भावः the state of a lord
or owner, ownership.
--मूल a.
originating in or derived from a
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">Page1162-c+ 55</a>]
master or lord.
--वात्सल्यं affection
for the husband or lord.
--सद्भावः {1}
existence of a master or owner. {2}
goodness of a master or lord.
--सेवा
{1} the service of a master. {2}
respect for a husband.
