<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनपुरं|हस्तिनपुर
हस्तिन(ना)पुरं N. of a city
founded by king Hastin, said to be
situated some fifty miles northeast
of the modern Delhi; it forms a
central scene of action in the
Mahābhārata; its other names are:
--गजाह्वय, नागसाह्वय, नागाह्व, हास्तिन.
