हार्य a.
1 To be taken or
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">Page1170-b+ 56</a>]
comveyed.
--2 To be borne or carried
on; यदूढया वारणराजहार्यया
Ku. 5. 70.
--3 To be taken away or
snatched off; R. 7. 67.
--4 To be
displaced or borne away (as by wind);
R. 16. 43.
--5 To be shaken (as
one's resolution); Ku. 5. 8.
--6
To be secured or won over, to be
attracted, conquered or influenced;
वहसि हि धनहार्यं पण्यभूतं शरीरं
Mk. 1. 31; Ku. 5. 53; Ms. 7. 217.
--7
To be seized or robbed;
Ms. 8. 417.
--र्यः
1 A snake.
--2 The
tree called Bibhītaka.
--3 The
dividend (in math.).
